**********************************************************************************			           	* FONT MANAGER * Version 3.2  	           	*			           	* Copyright Apple Computer, Inc. 1986-1991* All Rights Reserved		          	*			          	* V1.0	11/19/86	Cheryl Ewy	           	* V1.1	04/09/87	Bennet Marks, Cheryl Ewy       	* V2.0	05/14/87	Bennet Marks, Cheryl Ewy*** Version 2.3     	** 28 Apr 88	Harry Yee** Fixed problem w/FixFontMenu where the handle to the FMParam block was not* being locked and deref. at the correct place.** 15 Jun 88	Harry Yee** Prototype bit taken out of version #**** Version 2.4** 29 Jun 88	Steven Glass** Changed version number to 8204 for changes to scaling that make it run* in ROM.*** 14 Jul 88	Steven Glass** Two calls to GetWAP did not set the system/User flag correctly.  Instead they* were pushing the program ID.  This caused the ToolLocator to return random values* from the UserWAP Table.  This let the font manager use strange direct page* locations.  Its a wonder it ever worked.** The two routines that were affected are: DrawGuts and DrawSize.** 15 Jul 88	Steven Glass** LoadFont did not return valid fontstats if the font was not already in * memory.  This was because the LoadTheFont routine trashed the d-page location* TempPtr during the load.** 5 Dec 88	Sue Dumont** InstallFont would not recreate a font that had been purged out of memory.  This was* due to the fact that FindBestFit thought that the font was still hanging around.  Now,* the font handle is checked to verify that it is valid before making that assumption.** 10 Jan 89	Mensch* * Choose font had a bug that hung the system if certain windows had pending update* events. This was fixed by removing the use of taskmaster to perform auto updating* and replacing it with a check of the updatergn of the window itself and calling * the update routine.** 16 Jan 89	Mensch** ChooseFont modified to use newwindow2 call and new control types. This reduces* the size of the parameters handle allocated in RAM when the font manager starts* and allows for internationalization in the future.* ALSO fixed bug in install font, it did not always install the proper font.** 20 Jan 89	Mensch** Use new ROMResource stuff in misc tools for use with the choosefont call** 14 Feb 89 	Yee** TaskMask for ChooseFont dialog not correct. Bit 15 was clear which caused the choose* font window to deactivate when the mouse was clicked in a window that had an info bar.* This bottom window was then activated. Bit 15 is now set. BRC #41429.** 3/24/89	Mensch (Guest apperance by Dave Lyons)* * Fixed a bug in ReadFontLists that would cause the system to crash every now and then!** 19 Apr 89	Yee** Changed version number from 2.4 to 3.0** 6/12/89	Mensch** Fixed a bug in installfont. When you installed a scaled font that had been * installed before and purged, the new font would get a new entry in the font* list. This would cause orphaned fonts in memory. Now the new font re-uses the* previous entry in the font list.** 11/13/89	Mensch** Fixed a bug in FMStartup where it could leave partially digested font files on* disk. This could cause the system to crash. Now if anything goes wrong when * creating the font lists file, it will be destroyed, so as not to leave poop* on the disk.** 1/5/90	Mensch* Added code to put the watch cursor up when ChooseFont calls installFont and* the system waits.** 05 Apr 90	Yee* Fixed bug in FMStartup. FMStartup could return a bogus error if a buffer it got* to make OS calls crossed a bank boundary.** 28-Sep-90	Dave Lyons** Adding checks for reference number 0 before we do Close calls (when we needed a* new Font.Lists file and couldn't create one, we were doing Close(0) by* accident!).** Version $8303.** 25-Nov-90	Dave Lyons** Returns fmBadParmErr ($1b0d) if you're stupid enough to pass 0 for the user id* or direct-page address parameters to FMStartUp.** 6-Jan-91	Dave Lyons** Fixed a bug in Scale.asm (were losing bit 15 of owTOffset).* Made <FontSize a long instead of a word.  We now support >64K-big fonts on disk.* Optimized some lda #0/sta sequences into STZs.** 23-Jan-91	Dave Lyons** Doubled the maximum number of sizes displayed per family in ChooseFont from* 12 to 24.** 17-Feb-91	Dave Lyons** Change ChooseFont to use DoModalWindow.  Now supports key equivalents (Return,* ESC, Apple-period) and targetable list controls.* "Font size must be a number from 1 to 255" is now ErrorWindow($98) instead of* a hard-coded StopAlert call.  Optimized out a bunch of LDA/PHA into PEI.* Made GetDirEntry buffer 36 bytes long instead of 20.** Put extended task record storage inline (46 bytes).  Note that this makes* the Font Manager not ROMmable at the moment.** 17-Feb-91	Dave Lyons** Need to add new calls:*   $1D1B PreviewFontGlobals*   $1E1B GetFontPathname*   $1F1B AddFontByPathname** 24-Feb-91	Dave Lyons** Fixed ChooseFont direct-page use (broken 17-Feb when I decreased the amount* used, so that important stuff was getting overwritten by other Font Mgr calls!).** Changed the family name SortList call to pass 1 instead of 0 for sortProc, so* the list is now sorted case-insensitive.** 23-Apr-91	Dave Lyons* * ChooseFont--bop to the Family List if they type a bad key in one of the other* targetable items.** 25-Apr-91	Dave Lyons** Fixed FileName buffer to be long enough for 32-character file names.* Changed built pathnames to use colons instead of slashes, so that font* file names can contain slashes.  Changed AND #$000F to AND #$00FF so* we can have font file names longer than 15 characters.** 5-May-91	Dave Lyons** Fixed ChooseFont call to SelectMember2 (for selecting current font* size for new family) to not select anything if the size was not found* (was passing large value before, trashing memory).** 30-Sep-91	Dave Lyons** Now we use a real filetype/auxtype for the Font.List file ($5A;0008).** 4-Oct-91	Dave Lyons** ChooseFont re-checks the Plain box when no other boxes are checked.* Tabbing to a list doesn't rebuild the size list.** 2-Dec-91	Dave Lyons** Check for error on InflateTextBuffer call--don't make the font current* if we couldn't make the text buffers big enough!** Around LoadTheFont, set system preferences to prompt for disk, with no* Cancel button.  (MOD IS NOT ROMMABLE!)** 7-Dec-91	Dave Lyons** Changed GetAndFixPrefs to keep the Cancel button state, instead of* forcing no cancel button.** 16-Dec-91	Ben Koning** In MakeCurrent, there was a BCS to an RTS immediately after InflateTextBuffer* call.  The problem is that whoever called MakeCurrent (AddScaledFont, from* InstallFont) had already left the current grafport's font handle in a purgable* state, and thus when InflateTextBuffer fails with $0201=out of memory, its* memory manager calls have already managed to purge the current grafport's font.* The fix is to install the current system font handle, id, face, size upon* InflateTextBuffer tool error.  Also, this error now gets propagated from outside* of AddScaledFont.** 5-Feb-92	Dave Lyons** Fixed ChooseFont not to accidentally leave with an I-Beam cursor, or to leave* the I-Beam cursor up while it calls ErrorWindow with the bad-point-size* message.** 5-Feb-92pm	Dave Lyons** Version $0303 for 6.0 final.************************************************************************* 9-Mar-93	Steve Stephenson** Version $8304 for 6.0.1d14* Expanded the size list in ChooseFont to 96 members.  Added code to strip out duplicate* sizes from the list (due to different styles).  Changed many places of _DisposeHandle* to use a common subroutine.  Changed 56 occurrances of JMP to BRL to save on the OMF baggage.** 2-Apr-93	Steve Stephenson** Changed version to $0304 for 6.0.1 (final)**********************************************************************************	include 'all.macros'	include 'Special.macros'		string asis;------------------------------------------;; Gequ from procedure FMData;;------------------------------------------*** MaxSListCount	equ 12	;max # of members in Size list;MaxSListCount	equ 24	;max # of members in Size list (doubled 23-Jan-91 DAL)MaxSListCount	equ 96	;max # of members in Size list (re-re-doubled 8-Mar-93 SS);-----------------------------------------------;;   Imported address;;-----------------------------------------------	import strip	import oerrout	import endcall	import errout	import oendcall	import scalefont;-----------------------------------------------;;   Forward address	and entries;;-----------------------------------------------	ENTRY UnlockFMParams	entry sortsizes	ENTRY UnLock	ENTRY Lock	ENTRY MakeString	ENTRY UnLockItemList	ENTRY UnLockMDList	ENTRY IncItemPtr	ENTRY LockItemList	ENTRY IncMDPtr	ENTRY LockMDList	ENTRY BuildMDList	ENTRY GetEOF	ENTRY MakeCurrent	ENTRY UnLockFont	ENTRY LockFont	ENTRY CheckSysFont	ENTRY CheckNil	ENTRY AddScaledFont	ENTRY LoadTheFont	ENTRY StdEnd6	ENTRY StdErr6	ENTRY CheckFontID	ENTRY CheckHandle	ENTRY WriteFile	ENTRY CreateFile	ENTRY LockFMParams	ENTRY SetEOF	ENTRY SetMark	ENTRY GetDirEntry	ENTRY UnLockFileList	ENTRY UnLockNameList	ENTRY UnLockFamList	ENTRY UnLockIDList	ENTRY CloseFile	ENTRY ReadFile	ENTRY OpenFile	ENTRY CopyFileName	ENTRY IncFilePtr	ENTRY IncNamePtr	ENTRY IncFamPtr	ENTRY IncIDPtr	ENTRY CopyFamName	ENTRY LockFileList	ENTRY LockNameList	ENTRY LockFamList	ENTRY LockIDList	ENTRY StdEnd4	ENTRY LockBlock	ENTRY GetHandle	entry GetHandleXA	;6-Jan-91 DAL	ENTRY StdErr4	ENTRY DrawGuts	ENTRY SizeHit	ENTRY SizeList	ENTRY DrawSize	ENTRY FontHit	ENTRY GDENameBuf	ENTRY InstallWithStats	ENTRY FamNum2ItemID	ENTRY FMGetCurFID	ENTRY FMGetSysFID	ENTRY FMSetSysFont	ENTRY ItemID2FamNum	ENTRY ChooseFont	ENTRY FixFontMenu	ENTRY AddFontVar	ENTRY LoadSysFont	ENTRY LoadFont	ENTRY FindFontStats	ENTRY CountFonts	ENTRY SetPurgeStat	ENTRY InstallFont	ENTRY AddFamily	ENTRY GetFamNum	ENTRY GetFamInfo	ENTRY FindFamily	ENTRY CountFamilies	ENTRY oStdEnd0	ENTRY FMStatus	ENTRY FMReset	ENTRY FMVersion	ENTRY FMShutDown	ENTRY FMStartUp	ENTRY FMBootInit	ENTRY DisposeTheHandle****************************************************************** FONT MANAGER DATA	STRUCTURES******************************************************************---------------------------------------------------------------*  The Font Manager	keeps information about all of the available*  fonts in 4 different lists.  The ID List contains entries*  describing every	available font.  The Family List contains*  entries describing every distinct font family.  The Name	List*  contains entries	for each distinct font family name.  The*  File List contains entries for each font file on the system*  disk.  The structure of each of the 4 list entries is shown*  below. These structures are used throughout the Font Manager.*---------------------------------------------------------------*        ID List Entry	14 bytes**          Family #		2 bytes        0 (offset)*          Style		1 byte         2*          Size		1 byte         3*          Offset to Name List Entry	2 bytes        4*          Offset to File List Entry	2 bytes        6*          FontSpecBits	2 bytes        8*          Font Handle	4 bytes        10*---------------------------------------------------------------*        Fam List Entry	6 bytes**          Family #		2 bytes        0 (offset)*          Offset to Name List Entry	2 bytes        2*          FamSpecBits	2 bytes        4*---------------------------------------------------------------*        Name List Entry	2-26 bytes**          Family Name Length	1 byte*          Family Name	1-25 bytes*---------------------------------------------------------------*        File List Entry	2-16 bytes**          File Name Length	1 byte*          File Name	1-15 bytes*---------------------------------------------------------------*  The following data structure is used	only by*  the FixFontMenu and ChooseFont routines.*---------------------------------------------------------------*        MD List Entry	8 bytes**          Pointer to Name List Entry	4 bytes        0 (offset)*          List Manager Flags	1 byte         4*          Padding		1 byte         5*          Family #		2 bytes        6*---------------------------------------------------------------*  The following data structure is used	only by*  the ChooseFont routine.*---------------------------------------------------------------*        Size List Entry	5 bytes**          Size		2 bytes        0 (offset)*          Unused		2 bytes        2*          List Manager Flags	1 byte         4*---------------------------------------------------------------*  The following data structure is used	only by*  the FixFontMenu and ItemID2FamNum routines.*---------------------------------------------------------------*        Item List Entry	2 bytes**          Family #		2 bytes*---------------------------------------------------------------****************************************************************** FONT MANAGER DATA	DECLARATIONS******************************************************************---------------------------------------------------------------* Constants*---------------------------------------------------------------;;FMVerNum	equ $0304	;2-Apr-93 SSFMTSNum	equ $1B	;tool set num for Font ManagerInitErr	equ $1B01	;duplicate init callResetErr	equ $1B02	;can't reset Font ManagerActiveErr	equ $1B03	;Font Manager not activeNoFamErr	equ $1B04	;family not foundNoFontErr	equ $1B05	;font not foundMemErr	equ $1B06	;font not in memoryPurgeErr	equ $1B07	;system font cannot	be purgeableFamNumErr	equ $1B08	;illegal family numberSizeErr	equ $1B09	;illegal sizeNameErr	equ $1B0A	;illegal name lengthMenuErr	equ $1B0B	;FixFontMenu never called;added 2/10/87 - BHM:scaleSizeErr	equ $1B0C	;font can't be scaled that large;(must match ScaleFont definition)fmBadParmErr	equ $1b0d	;the user id or dp address was stupid (added 25-Nov-90 DAL);ProDOS	equ $E100A8	;ProDOS/16 entry vectorStackProDOS	equ $E100B0	;ProDOS/16 stack-based entry vectorOpenCall	equ $10	;ProDOS/16 call numberReadCall	equ $12	;           "CloseCall	equ $14	;           "SetMarkCall	equ $16	;           "GetEOFCall	equ $19	;           "CreateCall	equ $01	;           "WriteCall	equ $13	;           "SetEOFCall	equ $18	;           "GDECall	equ $1C	;           "DestroyCall	equ $02ButtonItem	equ 10	;item type for dialog managerStatTextItem	equ 15+$8000	;           "KeyDownEvt	equ 3	;event codeautoKeyEvt	equ 5	;event code (DAL)ListPartCode	equ $88	;part code for listMessage	equ 2	;offset into TaskRecWhere	equ 10	;         "Modifiers	equ 14	;         "TaskMask	equ 20	;         "DirNameLen	equ 14	;length of '*:System:Fonts'MaxNameLen	equ 25	;max length of font's family nameBlockSize	equ 512Illegal	equ $FFFF	;illegal family numberFontType	equ $C8	;filetype for font filesMemOnlyBit	equ $0001	;FontSpecBitsRealOnlyBit	equ $0002AnyFamBit	equ $0004AnyStyleBit	equ $0008AnySizeBit	equ $0010MemBit	equ $0001	;FontStatBitsUnrealBit	equ $0002ApFamBit	equ $0004ApVarBit	equ $0008PurgeBit	equ $0010NotDiskBit	equ $0020NotFoundBit	equ $8000BaseOnlyBit	equ $0020	;FamSpecBits;ApFamBit      equ $0004	;FamStatBitsNotBaseBit	equ $0020;NotFoundBit   equ $8000NotMemBit	equ $FFFE	;all bits set except MemBitUnPurgeable	equ $FFEF	;all bits set except PurgeBit;;added 2/10/87 - BHM:dontScaleBit	equ $0001	;(see scaleWord input in InstallFont)currFlag	equ $0001	;make font current (see LoadTheFont)notCurrFlag	equ $FFFEnewMemFlag	equ $0002	;(see LoadTheFont)oldMemFlag	equ $0004	;(see LoadTheFont);;                COPY new.cons;*****************************************************************************			               **  file NEW.CONS			               **			               **    started 8/31/87		               **    Bennet Marks  x6245		               **			               **  This file contains some new constants needed by the FMStartUp speed-up  **  experiment.  Also included are offsets used to make ProDOS stack-based  **  calls.			               **			               *****************************************************************************;****************************************	                  **  11/10/87  1:20 pm                  **  BHM  x6245	                  **	                  ****************************************;;FONT.LISTS format version number:;FLVerHi	equ $0000FLVerLo	equ $0001;;offsets to data in	the FONT.LISTS file:;oRomFamNum	equ 4oRomStyle	equ oRomFamNum+2oRomSize	equ oRomStyle+2oIDCount	equ oRomSize+2oFamCount	equ oIDCount+2oIDListSize	equ oFamCount+2oFamListSize	equ oIDListSize+2oNameListSize	equ oFamListSize+2oFileListSize	equ oNameListSize+2oTimeListSize	equ oFileListSize+2;FLFileHeadLen	equ oTimeListSize+2;;and some other constants:;GDENameBufSize	equ 36	;for the name buffer (was 20, 17-Feb-91 DAL)FileNotFound	equ $46EndOfDir	equ $61BinFile	equ $06;;*---------------------------------------------------------------* Font Manager Zero	Page*---------------------------------------------------------------FMZBase	equ 0TempHandle	equ FMZBase	;the following handles must be inFileHandle	equ TempHandle+4	;this orderIDHandle	equ FileHandle+4FamHandle	equ IDHandle+4NameHandle	equ FamHandle+4FontHandle	equ NameHandle+4BlockHandle	equ FontHandle+4MDHandle	equ BlockHandle+4ItemHandle	equ MDHandle+4FMParamHandle	equ ItemHandle+4	;added 11/10/87 - BHM x6245TempPtr	equ FMParamHandle+4	;the following pointers must be inFilePtr	equ TempPtr+4	;this orderIDPtr	equ FilePtr+4FamPtr	equ IDPtr+4NamePtr	equ FamPtr+4FontPtr	equ NamePtr+4BlockPtr	equ FontPtr+4MDPtr	equ BlockPtr+4ItemPtr	equ MDPtr+4FMParamPtr	equ ItemPtr+4	;added 11/10/87 - BHM x6245SavedFilePtr	equ FMParamPtr+4	;the following pointers must be inSavedIDPtr	equ SavedFilePtr+4	;this orderSavedFamPtr	equ SavedIDPtr+4SavedNamePtr	equ SavedFamPtr+4IDListSize	equ SavedNamePtr+4FamListSize	equ IDListSize+2NameListSize	equ FamListSize+2ItemListSize	equ NameListSize+2	;** added 2-25-87 CAE **IDCount	equ ItemListSize+2FamCount	equ IDCount+2;****  CHANGED 11/4/87:;all the Font Manager's ProDOS calls (except GetDirEntry) now share a common;block of 0-page for their parameter blocks.  Note that the	reference numbers;(OpenRef, ReadRef,	etc.) are actually the same 0-page location.  In partic-;ular, after an OpenFile call is done, the new ref number is in the right;position for a subsequent ReadFile call. - BHM  x6245  11/4/87;ProDOSParams	equ FamCount+2;;Open call:OpenRef	equ ProDOSParams	;reference numberOpenPtr	equ OpenRef+2	;ptr to pathnameOpenBuf	equ OpenPtr+4	;unused by Font Manager;Read call:ReadRef	equ ProDOSParams	;reference numberReadPtr	equ ReadRef+2	;ptr to data bufferReadSize	equ ReadPtr+4	;number of bytes to	readReadActual	equ ReadSize+4	;number of bytes actually read;Close call (whew!):CloseRef	equ ProDOSParams	;reference number;GetEOF and SetEOF calls:EOFRef	equ ProDOSParams	;reference numberEOFSize	equ EOFRef+2	;EOF (new or returned result);GetMark and SetMark calls:MarkRef	equ ProDOSParams	;refernce numberMarkLoc	equ MarkRef+2	;mark (new or returned result);Write call:WriteRef	equ ProDOSParamsWriteBuf	equ WriteRef+2WriteReq	equ WriteBuf+4WriteTrans	equ WriteReq+4;Create call:CRNamePtr	equ ProDOSParamsCRAccess	equ CRNamePtr+4CRFileType	equ CRAccess+2CRAuxType	equ CRFileType+2CRStore	equ CRAuxType+4CRDate	equ CRStore+2CRTime	equ CRDate+2;Destroy call:KillNamePtr	equ ProDOSParams;****  end of changes to ProDOS parameter blocks - BHM  x6245  11/4/87;;note that the parameter blocks above all use less than 20 bytes;MenuMade	equ ProDOSParams+20	;so this is safeStartingID	equ MenuMade+2ProgID	equ StartingID+2SysFontID	equ ProgID+2RomFbrExtent	equ SysFontID+4OldStats	equ RomFBRExtent+2	;added 12/16/87 - BHM  x6245;(for use by InstallWithStats);added 1/11/88 - BHM  x6245temp1Ptr	equ OldStats+2temp2Ptr	equ temp1Ptr+4;the following locations are used to hold information that,	in the RAM;of this tool, were	kept in the data segment.  Some also subsume 0-page;locations that used to be private to ChooseFont - BHM  x6245  1/25/88ScreenMode	equ temp2Ptr+4WindPtr	equ ScreenMode+2LineHndl	equ WindPtr+4Temp	equ LineHndl+4;; Equates for ChooseFont item ID'sMDListID	equ 1SizeListID	equ 2SizeEditID	equ 3OKID	equ 4CancelID	equ 5; these next style ID's must be in order...PlainSID	equ 6BoldSID	equ 7ItalicSID	equ 8UnderSID	equ 9OutlineSID	equ 10ShadowSID	equ 11LastSID	equ 12;stat1ID	equ 12stat2ID	equ 13stat3ID	equ 14;; RefCon Equates for ChooseFont controlsuseNILHit	equ 0useFontHit	equ 1useSizeHit	equ 2useOtherHit	equ 3useOKHit	equ 4useCancelHit	equ 5usePlainHit	equ 6useStyleHit	equ 7****************************************************************** FONT MANAGER CALL	TABLE*****************************************************************	EXPORT FMCallTableFMCallTable	PROC	import NewInstallFont	import NewInstallWithStatsTheStart	DC.L (TheEnd-TheStart)/4 	;num calls + 1	DC.L FMBootInit-1	DC.L FMStartUp-1	DC.L FMShutDown-1	DC.L FMVersion-1	DC.L FMReset-1	DC.L FMStatus-1	DC.L oStdEnd0-1	DC.L oStdEnd0-1	DC.L CountFamilies-1	DC.L FindFamily-1	DC.L GetFamInfo-1	DC.L GetFamNum-1	DC.L AddFamily-1	DC.L NewInstallFont-1	DC.L SetPurgeStat-1	DC.L CountFonts-1	DC.L FindFontStats-1	DC.L LoadFont-1	DC.L LoadSysFont-1	DC.L AddFontVar-1	DC.L FixFontMenu-1	DC.L ChooseFont-1	DC.L ItemID2FamNum-1	DC.L FMSetSysFont-1	DC.L FMGetSysFID-1	DC.L FMGetCurFID-1	DC.L FamNum2ItemID-1 ;** added 2-25-87 CAE **;the following call	was added late 12/87;name changed 1/4/87 - BHM  x6245	DC.L NewInstallWithStats-1TheEnd	ENDP	ENTRY FMDataFMData	PROC	Import StyleHit	Import CancelHit	Import OKHit	Import PlainHit	*---------------------------------------------------------------* Font Manager Data*---------------------------------------------------------------**  The following are templates, so they'll get copied over into*  RAM for later use:**	ENTRY FMParamsFMParams*-------------- GetDirEntry Parameter Block --------------------	ENTRY GDERefGDERef	DC.W 0	ENTRY GDEReservedGDEReserved	DC.W 0	ENTRY GDEBaseGDEBase	DC.W 1	ENTRY GDEDisplaceGDEDisplace	DC.W 1	ENTRY GDENameBufPtrGDENameBufPtr	DC.L GDENameBuf	ENTRY GDEEntryGDEEntry	DC.W 0	ENTRY GDEFileTypeGDEFileType	DC.W 0	ENTRY GDEEOFGDEEOF	DC.L 0	ENTRY GDEBlockCountGDEBlockCount	DC.L 0	ENTRY GDECreateTimeGDECreateTime	ds.b 8	ENTRY GDEModTimeGDEModTime	ds.b 8	ENTRY GDEAccessGDEAccess	DC.W 0	ENTRY GDEAuxTypeGDEAuxType	DC.L 0	ENTRY GDEFileSysIDGDEFileSysID	DC.W 0;name buffer:	ENTRY GDENameBufGDENameBuf	DC.W GDENameBufSize	ENTRY GDENameLenGDENameLen	DC.W 0GDEName	ds.b GDENameBufSize-4*-------------- Font Filename Stuff ----------------------------	ENTRY DirNameDirName	DC.B 0	;length byte	DC.B '*:System:Fonts'	ENTRY FileName***FileName	DC.B '/               'FileName	dc.b ':                                '  ;25-Apr-91 DAL;	ENTRY FLFileNameFLFileName	DC.B 10	DC.B 'Font.Lists'*-------------- Dummy Menu Item for FixFontMenu ----------------	ENTRY DummyItemDummyItem	DC.B '  '	;place holder	DC.B ' \H'	;dummy string	ENTRY DummyItemIDDummyItemID	DC.W 0	;item ID	DC.B 0	;terminator	ENTRY StyleItemRectStyleItemRect	ds.b 8*-------------- List Stuff for ChooseFont and FixFontMenu ------	ENTRY MDListRectMDListRect	ds.b 8	;list's enclosing rectangle	ENTRY MDListSizeMDListSize	DC.W 0	;# of members in list	DC.W 6	;view size	DC.W 2	;type of members	DC.W 1	;starting member	DC.L 0	;space for list control's handle	DC.L 0	;address of routine	to draw members	DC.W 10	;height of member in pixels	DC.W 8	;size of each member record	ENTRY MDListPtrMDListPtr	DC.L 0	;pointer to member list	DC.L FontHit	;refcon	DC.L 0	;address of color table for scroll bar;	ENTRY SizeListRectSizeListRect	ds.b 8	;list's enclosing rectangle	ENTRY SizeListSizeSizeListSize	DC.W 0	;# of members in list	DC.W 6	;view size	DC.W 2	;type of members	DC.W 1	;starting member	DC.L 0	;space for list control's handle	DC.L DrawSize	;address of routine	to draw members	DC.W 10	;height of member in pixels	DC.W 5	;size of each member record	ENTRY SizeListPtrSizeListPtr	DC.L SizeList	;pointer to member list	DC.L SizeHit	;refcon	DC.L 0	;address of color table for scroll bar	ENTRY WindTemplatesWindTemplates	dc.L $0FFF1B01	; 320 mode choosefont window res ID	dc.L 0	; 320 mode alert window	dc.L $0FFF1B02	; 640 mode choosefont window res ID	dc.L 0	; 640 mode alert window		ENTRY SizeList*** SizeList	ds.b 60	;space for 12 Size list membersSizeList	ds.b 5*MaxSListCount  ;23-Jan-91 DAL	ENTRY StrLen	ENTRY TheStrStrLen	ds.b 1TheStr	ds.b 3	ENTRY EndOfFMParamsEndOfFMParams;; ROM only data follows***	entry AlertRect***AlertRect	dc.W 35,35,85,285***	dc.W 35,195,85,445******	ENTRY OKStr***OKStr	str 'OK'	if 0 then	;DAL 23-Jan-91 -- why is this stuff here in TOOL027?		;We're getting it from GetROMResource these days	entry OtherRectOtherRect	dc.W 99,205,112,241	dc.W 99,205,112,241		ENTRY StrDataStrData	ENTRY StylePtrsStylePtrs	DC.L Style1Str	DC.L Style2Str	DC.L Style3Str	DC.L Style4Str	DC.L Style5Str	DC.L Style6Str	ENTRY CancelStrCancelStr	str 'Cancel'	ENTRY Style1Str	ENTRY Style2Str	ENTRY Style3Str	ENTRY Style4Str	ENTRY Style5Str	ENTRY Style6StrStyle1Str	str 'Plain'Style2Str	str 'Bold'Style3Str	str 'Italic'Style4Str	str 'Underline'Style5Str	str 'Outline'Style6Str	str 'Shadow'	endif	;end of stuff we don't need (comes from GetROMResource);	ENTRY AlertStr;TempStart;AlertStr	DC.B TempEnd-TempStart-1 ; $29	         ;EndAlertStr-AlertStr-1;	DC.B 'Font size must be a';	DC.B $0D;	DC.B 'number from 1 to 255.';	ENTRY EndAlertStr;EndAlertStr;TempEnd	ENDP;                COPY init****************************************************************** FMBootInit*****************************************************************	ENTRY FMBootInitFMBootInit	PROC	brl oStdEnd0	ENDP****************************************************************** FMStartUp*****************************************************************	ENTRY FMStartUpFMStartUp	PROCEntryLength	equ TempEntriesInBlock	equ EntryLength+2EntryCount	equ EntriesInBlock+2NumFiles	equ EntryCount+2NumFonts	equ NumFiles+2FileCount	equ NumFonts+2Mult2	equ FileCount+2Mult8	equ Mult2+2Mult16	equ Mult8+2RomInfoRec	equ Mult16+2	;the following items MUST appearRomFamNum	equ RomInfoRec	;in this orderRomStyle	equ RomFamNum+2RomSize	equ RomStyle+2RomFontHndl	equ RomSize+2RomNamePtr	equ RomFontHndl+4RomExtent	equ RomNamePtr+4;;added 8/31/87fNamePtr	equ RomExtent+2currFNamePtr	equ fNamePtr+4;fNameLen	equ currFNamePtr+4currFNameLen	equ fNameLen+2errCode	equ currFNameLen+2FLFileRef	equ errCode+2FONTSDirRef	equ FLFileRef+2FileListSize	equ FONTSDirRef+2NumFontFiles	equ FileListSize+2;added 9/24/87TimeListSize	equ NumFontFiles+2TimeHandle	equ TimeListSize+2TimePtr	equ TimeHandle+4SavedTimePtr	equ TimePtr+4fTimePtr	equ SavedTimePtr+4;end of additions -	BHM  x6245;***	cmp #0	;already initialized?	tax	;optimized 25-Nov-90 DAL	beq @Doit	;no	ldx #InitErr	;yes - so return error@stupidErr	ldy #4	;param size	jml oerrout@Doit*** added 25-Nov-90 DAL*** return error for stupid direct-page or user id parameters	ldx #fmBadParmErr	lda 7,s	beq @stupidErr	lda 9,s	beq @stupidErr*** end of 25-Nov-90 DAL	phd	lda 9,s	;get zero page address	tcd	ldx #$FEZPLoop	stz <FMZBase,x	;clear zero page	dex	dex	bpl ZPLoop	lda 11,s	;get program ID	sta <ProgID	;and save;;get RAM space for some mutable FM data, and move them in:	jsr SetUpFMParams	bcc GotFMParams	tax	;error code	brl StdErr4GotFMParams;;get a buffer for block reads:	lda #BlockSize	;512 bytes	jsr GetHandle	;get space to do block reads into	bcc GotMem	sta <errCode	brl Error1	;return the error;GotMem	sta <BlockHandle	;get handle to block	stx <BlockHandle+2;	jsr LockBlock;	jsr GetListHandles	bcc GotListHandles	sta <errCode	brl Error1aGotListHandles*******************************************************************************  Error-handling changed here and below so that ProDOS errors in handling*  FONT.LISTS do not abort the start-up.  (In particular, trying to create*  and/or update FONT.LISTS when the system disk is write-protected does not*  generate an error; FONT.LISTS is just forgotten about is	those cases.)**  Bennet Marks  x6245  1/7/88******************************************************************************	jsr OpenFLFile	;will also create it, if need be	bcc GotFLFile;some error condition - treat FONT.LISTS as invalid (i.e., useless);	jsr OpenFONTSDir	bcc FLFileNotValid	;because it's empty	sta <errCode	brl Error2aGotFLFile		;and it's open, too	jsr OpenFONTSDir	bcc GotFONTSDir	sta <errCode	brl Error3GotFONTSDir	jsr CheckFLFile	bcc FLFileGood;some error condition - FONT.LISTS useless;FLFileNotValid;FONTS open, marked	at beginning & FONT.LISTS open, empty;;FONT.LISTS didn't pass its validity test, so we have to make;the lists "the old-fashioned way";	jsr GetFileNames	bcc GotFileNames	brl Error5;GotFileNames	jsr SetUpFontInfo	bcc FontListsOK	sta <errCode	brl Error6;FontListsOK	jsr UpdateFLFile;ignore any errors - just because we can't;update FONT.LISTS doesn't mean we should quit;; 11/13/89 Mensch; But it does mean that the file that was written out is probably BAD!; Since this could easily be the case, we test for errors here and delete the file; if any errors occured in the process of writing the file.; This should fix bugs where bad font.lists were being created 	bcc FLFileDone	jsr KillBadFLFile	; font list file somehow bad, kill it!FLFileDone	bra WeAreDone;;FLFileGood;FONT.LISTS passed the validity tests, so we trust the rest	of its info	jsr ReadFontLists	bcc GotFontLists	sta <errCode	brl Error8;GotFontLists;all done, so:;WeAreDone;	jsr CloseFLFile	jsr CloseFONTSDir;	jsr UnlockFMParams;	lxy <BlockHandle	;8-Mar-93 SS	jsr DisposeTheHandle;(NOTE:  later, we may actually want to	keep the param block around until;FMShutDown.  For this we need another permanent handle - but we'll get back;0-page space now used for ProDOS call parameters.);	lxy <TimeHandle	;8-Mar-93 SS	jsr DisposeTheHandle;	lda 9,s	;get zero page address	PushWord #0	PushWord #FMTSNum	PushWord #0	pha	_SetWAP	;set work area pointer	brl StdEnd4;;Error8Error7Error6Error5Error4	jsr CloseFONTSDir;Error3Error2a	jsr CloseFLFile;Error2	lxy <FileHandle	;8-Mar-93 SS	jsr DisposeTheHandle	lxy <IDHandle	;8-Mar-93 SS	jsr DisposeTheHandle	lxy <FamHandle	;8-Mar-93 SS	jsr DisposeTheHandle	lxy <NameHandle	;8-Mar-93 SS	jsr DisposeTheHandle	lxy <TimeHandle	;8-Mar-93 SS	jsr DisposeTheHandle;Error1a	lxy <BlockHandle	;8-Mar-93 SS	jsr DisposeTheHandle;Error1	lxy <FMParamHandle	;8-Mar-93 SS	jsr DisposeTheHandle;	ldx <errCode	brl StdErr4****************************************	                  **  end FMStartUp	                  **	                  ****************************************;******************************************************************************			                **  subroutine SetupFontInfo		                **			                ******************************************************************************;****************************************	                  **  9/8/87  5:40 pm	                  **  BHM  x6245	                  **	                  ****************************************;SetupFontInfo;	jsr LockIDList	jsr LockFamList	jsr LockNameList	jsr LockFileList	jsr SaveListPtrs	;save ptrs to all 4	lists;Set up first entry	in each list for ROM font.  At FMStartUp time,;QuickDraw system font must be the ROM font so set SysFontID to ID of ROM font.	PushZPtr <RomInfoRec	_GetRomFont	lda <RomExtent	sta <RomFbrExtent	;save for GrowTextBuf routine	lda <RomFamNum	;get ROM font's fam #	sta [<FamPtr]	;store in fam entry	sta [<IDPtr]	;and ID entry	sta <SysFontID	;and Sys font info	lda <RomSize	;get ROM font's size	xba	ora <RomStyle	;OR with ROM font's style	ldy #2	sta [<IDPtr],y	;store style/size word in ID entry	sta <SysFontID+2	;and Sys font info	lda #0	;zero out fields in	ID and fam entries	sta [<FamPtr],y	;offset to famname entry	iny	iny	sta [<FamPtr],y	;info word	sta [<IDPtr],y	;offset to famname entry	iny	iny	sta [<IDPtr],y	;offset to filename	entry	iny	iny	lda #MemBit	sta [<IDPtr],y	;info word (MemBit set)	lda <RomStyle	;get ROM font's style	beq RomPlain	;it's plain	lda #NotBaseBit	ldy #4	sta [<FamPtr],y	;it's not plain so set 'NotBaseBit'RomPlain		;	ldy #10	lda <RomFontHndl	;get handle to ROM font	sta [<IDPtr],y	;store in ID entry	iny	iny	lda <RomFontHndl+2	sta [<IDPtr],y	lda <RomNamePtr	;get ptr to ROM font name	sta <TempPtr	lda <RomNamePtr+2	sta <TempPtr+2GotName	jsr CopyFamName	;copy ROM font name	into famname list	jsr IncIDPtr	jsr IncFamPtr	jsr IncNamePtr	jsr IncFilePtr;Read in the first block of each font file.  Create an ID entry for each font;and Family and Name entries for each distinct family.	stz <FileCount	;# font files processed	lda #1	sta <FamCount	;# of font families	(count ROM font)	sta <IDCount	;# of fonts (count ROM font)	lda <NumFonts	bne FileLoop	brl Done2	;quit if no font files to processFileLoop	jsr CopyFileName	;copy file name into pathname string**** changed to use	FMParams block - BHM  x6245  11/12/87	lda <FMParamPtr	clc	adc #(DirName-FMParams) ;store ptr to pathname of	sta <OpenPtr	;font file in OPEN param	lda <FMParamPtr+2	adc #0	sta <OpenPtr+2	jsr OpenFile	;open the font file	bcc ReadBlock	rts;ReadBlock;the Open was just done, so the ref number is in place for reading	lda #BlockSize	sta <ReadSize***	lda #0***	sta <ReadSize+2	stz <ReadSize+2	;6-Jan-91 DAL	lda <BlockPtr	sta <ReadPtr	lda <BlockPtr+2	sta <ReadPtr+2;(actually, you don't have to do all that, at least not every time -;but I'm just getting used to this stuff - BHM  9/4/87);	jsr ReadFile	;read first block of font file	bcc NewID;	rts	;return the error;create a new entry	in the ID list for this fontNewID	sec	lda <FilePtr	;calc offset to filename entry in list	sbc <SavedFilePtr	ldy #6	sta [<IDPtr],y	;store in ID entry	lda [<BlockPtr]	;get font's famname length	and #$00FF	inc a	;add 1 for the length byte itself	inc a	;add 2 to skip 'offset to MF' field	inc a	tay	;offset to ID in the font file	lda [<BlockPtr],y	;get font's family # from file	sta [<IDPtr]	;store in ID entry	iny	iny	lda [<BlockPtr],y	;get font's style word from file	and #$00FF	;mask off hi byte	pha	;save on stack	iny	iny	lda [<BlockPtr],y	;get font's size word from file	and #$00FF	;mask off hi byte	xba	;swap bytes	ora 1,s	;OR with style word	ldy #2	sta [<IDPtr],y	;store style/size word in ID entry	pla	;clean up stack	lda #0	ldy #8	sta [<IDPtr],y	;zero out info word	in ID entry	iny	iny	sta [<IDPtr],y	;zero out font handle in ID entry	iny	iny	sta [<IDPtr],y;check if this font's family already has an entry in the Fam list	ldx #0	;# of fam entries checked	ldy #0FamLoop	lda [<SavedFamPtr],y ;get fam #	cmp [<IDPtr]	;match?	beq GotFam	;yes - so already entry for this fam #	tya	clc	adc #6	tay	;create offset to next fam entry	inx	cpx <FamCount	;have we checked all fam entries?	bne FamLoop	;no	bra NewFam	;yes - so it's a new fam #GotFam	iny	iny	phy	;save Y on stack	lda [<SavedFamPtr],y ;get offset to famname	ldy #4	sta [<IDPtr],y	;store famname offset in ID entry	ldy #2	lda [<IDPtr],y	;get style/size of font	ply	;retrieve previous value of Y	and #$00FF	;mask off size byte	bne NotPlain	;branch if font is not plain	iny	;font is plain	iny	lda #0	sta [<SavedFamPtr],y ;clear info word for fam entryNotPlain	brl NextFile;create new entries	in the Fam list and	the Name list for this font's familyNewFam	sec	lda <NamePtr	sbc <SavedNamePtr	;calculate offset to famname in list	ldy #2	sta [<FamPtr],y	;store in fam entry	ldy #4	sta [<IDPtr],y	;and ID entry	lda <BlockPtr	sta <TempPtr	lda <BlockPtr+2	sta <TempPtr+2	jsr CopyFamName	;copy famname into famname list	lda [<IDPtr]	;get family #	sta [<FamPtr]	;and save in fam list	ldy #2	lda [<IDPtr],y	;get style/size of font	and #$00FF	;mask off size byte	beq Plain	;branch if font is plain	lda #NotBaseBitPlain	ldy #4	sta [<FamPtr],y	;set info word in fam entry	inc <FamCount	;# of font families	jsr IncNamePtr	jsr IncFamPtrNextFile	jsr CloseFile	;close the font file;(there's been no ProDOS action since Opening and Reading, so;the ref number is still right.)	bcc CloseOK	rtsCloseOK	jsr IncFilePtr	jsr IncIDPtr	inc <IDCount	inc <FileCount	lda <FileCount	;get # font files processed	cmp <NumFonts	;done with all font	files?	beq Done2	;yes	brl FileLoop	;no - so continueDone2	jsr UnLockIDList	jsr UnLockFamList	jsr UnLockNameList	jsr UnLockFileList	jsr ShrinkLists	;shrink all lists to correct size	rts****************************************	                  **  end SetupFontInfo                  **	                  ****************************************;******************************************************************************			                **  subroutine SizeLists		                **			                **    started 8/27/86		                **    Bennet Marks  x6245		                **			                **  This subroutine re-sizes the Font Manager's lists to the maximum size    **  needed to accept	the information read in from all the font files in      **  FONTS.  This is done after FONT.LISTS has failed the validity test (if   **  FONT.LISTS was valid, we would read the lists and their exact sizes in   **  from there).			                **			                **  The sizing is based on the number of	font files, and the	maximum allowed **  lengths for font	family names and file names.  The lists	will be shrunk  **  after the actual	space needed is known.	                **			                **  If the SizeLists	succeeds, it returns with carry clear; otherwise it     **  returns with carry set and the error	code in the acc.  SizeLists returns **  by an RTS, and does not have a separate entry point; it's part of        **  FMStartUp.			                **			                ******************************************************************************;****************************************	                  **  9/24/87  12:45 pm                  **  BHM  x6245	                  **	                  ****************************************;SizeLists	PushWord #0	;for high word of size	lda <NumFiles	;get # of files in FONTS	inc a	;add 1 for ROM font	asl a	sta <Mult2	;multiply by 2 and save result	asl a	asl a	sta <Mult8	;multiply by 8 and save result	asl a	sta <Mult16	;multiply by 16 and	save result	clc	lda <Mult16	adc <Mult8	adc <Mult2	pha	;low word of size	PushZLong <NameHandle	_SetHandleSize	bcc SizedNameHndl	rtsSizedNameHndl	jsr UnlockFileList	jsr UnlockTimeList***	PushWord #0	;high word of size*	lda <Mult16	;low word of size*	pha***	pei <Mult16*** added 25-Apr-91 DAL	pha	pha	pea 33	pei <NumFiles	;fileHandle can need 33*NumFiles bytes	_Multiply*** end of 25-Apr-91 DAL	PushZLong <FileHandle	_SetHandleSize	bcc SizedFileHndl	rtsSizedFileHndl	PushWord #0	;high word of size	sec	lda <Mult16	sbc <Mult2	;low word of size	pha	PushZLong <IDHandle	_SetHandleSize	bcc SizedIDHndl	rtsSizedIDHndl	PushWord #0	;hi	sec	lda <Mult8	sbc <Mult2	;low	pha	PushZLong <FamHandle	_SetHandleSize	bcc SizedFamHandle	rtsSizedFamHandle	PushWord #0	PushWord <Mult16	PushZLong <TimeHandle	_SetHandleSize	rts****************************************	                  **  end SizeLists	                  **	                  ****************************************;*****************************************************************************			               **  subroutine ShrinkLists		               **			               *****************************************************************************;****************************************	                  **  9/28/87  2:20 pm	                  **  BHM  x6245	                  **	                  ****************************************;ShrinkLists;	sec	lda <FilePtr	sbc <SavedFilePtr	;calculate final size of filename list	sta <FileListSize	PushWord #0	;hi word of size	pha	;lo word of size	PushZLong <FileHandle ;handle to list	_SetHandleSize	;shrink list to correct size	sec	lda <NamePtr	sbc <SavedNamePtr	;calculate final size of famname list	sta <NameListSize	;and save	Pushword #0	;hi word of size	pha	;lo word of size	PushZLong <NameHandle ;handle to list	_SetHandleSize	;shrink list to correct size	sec	lda <FamPtr	sbc <SavedFamPtr	;calculate final size of family list	sta <FamListSize	;and save	PushWord #0	;hi word of size	pha	;lo word of size	PushZLong <FamHandle ;handle to list	_SetHandleSize	;shrink list to correct size	sec	lda <IDPtr	sbc <SavedIDPtr	;calculate final size of ID list	sta <IDListSize	;and save	PushWord #0	;hi word of size	pha	;lo word of size	PushZLong <IDHandle	;handle to list	_SetHandleSize	;shrink list to correct size;;time list is handled in GetFileNames	rts;-----------------------------------------------------------------------------SaveListPtrs	ldx #14Loop	lda <FilePtr,x	sta <SavedFilePtr,x	dex	dex	bpl Loop;;time list is handles in GetFileNames	rts;******************************************************************************			                **  subroutine OpenFONTSDir		                **			                **    started 8/27/87		                **    Bennet Marks  x6245		                **			                **  This subroutine opens the subdirectory *:SYSTEM:FONTS, which is supposed **  to contain all font files (that the Font Manager is to handle) and the   **  file FONT.LISTS.	 If it succeeds, it	saves the subdirectory's reference  **  number in FONTSDirRef, and returns with the carry clear;	otherwise it    **  returns with the	carry set and the error number in the acc.              **			                **  Currently, OpenFONTSDir returns with	an RTS, and does not have a         **  separate entry point; it's just part of FMStartUp.                       **			                ******************************************************************************;****************************************	                  **  2/9/88 (Happy Birthday, Steve!     **  BHM  x6245	                  **	                  ****************************************;OpenFONTSDir		;;****  changed to use FMParams block - BHM  x6245  11/12/87;	ldy #(DirName-FMParams)	lda [<FMParamPtr],y	;get first word of font subdir-	and #$FF00	;ectory name and clear lenght byte	ora #DirNameLen	;set length to proper value	sta [<FMParamPtr],y	;and save	lda <FMParamPtr	clc	adc #(DirName-FMParams) ;store ptr to name of font subdirectory	sta <OpenPtr	;in OPEN params;correction added 2/9/88               	lda <FMParamPtr+2	adc #0	sta <OpenPtr+2;end of correction - BHM  x6245  2/9/88	jsr OpenFile	;open the font subdirectory file	bcc OpenOK	rts	;back with error;OpenOK		;	lda <OpenRef	sta <FONTSDirRef	rts****************************************	                  **  end OpenFONTSDir	                  **	                  ****************************************;******************************************************************************			                **  subroutine GetFileNames		                **			                **    started 8/27/87		                **    Bennet Marks  x6245		                **			                **  This subroutine is called when FONT.LISTS doesn't pass the validity      **  test.  It goes out to the disk and constructs a list of all font file    **  names, so that a	later subroutine (SetUpFontInfo) can open them all,     **  one at a time, and construct the other lists the Font Manager needs.     **			                **  GetFontNames assumes the FONTS subdirectory has already been opened.     **  It returns with an RTS, and does not	have a separate entry point; it's   **  just part of FMStartUp.		                **			                ******************************************************************************;****************************************	                  **  11/10/87  3:10 pm                  **  BHM  x6245	                  **	                  ****************************************;****************************************	                  **  Changed to use GetDirEntry         **  - BHM  9/15/87	                  **	                  **  Now gets create & mod times &      **  dates (maybe we should rename it)  **  - BHM 9/24/87	                  **	                  ****************************************;GetFileNames		;;;use GetDirEntry to	get the number of active files in FONTS;	lda <FONTSDirRef	sta [<FMParamPtr]	;trust me;	lda #0	ldy #(GDEBase-FMParams)	sta [<FMParamPtr],y	iny	iny	sta [<FMParamPtr],y;	jsr GetDirEntry;;quick like rabbit set GDE default params back, just in case;	lda #1	ldy #(GDEBase-FMParams)	sta [<FMParamPtr],y	iny	iny	sta [<FMParamPtr],y;	bcc GotNumFiles	lda #0	; if an error occured, zero out the number of files	ldy #(GDEEntry-FMParams)	sta [<FMParamPtr],y; and drop right thru to the rest of the routine now ...;GotNumFiles		;	ldy #(GDEEntry-FMParams)	lda [<FMParamPtr],y	sta <NumFiles	;number of active files in FONTS;	jsr SizeLists	bcc GotLists	rts;GotLists		;	jsr LockFileList	jsr LockTimeList;this seems to be a	good place to save TimePtr	lda <TimePtr	sta <SavedTimePtr	lda <TimePtr+2	sta <SavedTimePtr+2;	stz <NumFonts	;# of font files (not ROM font);;create "dummy" file entry for ROM font	and;application fonts to point to;	lda #1	sta [<filePtr]	lda #0	ldy #2	sta [<filePtr],y;	jsr IncFilePtr;;create dummy entry	in TimeList (just for consistency)	ldy #14	lda #0NextTimeWord	sta [<TimePtr],y	dey	dey	bpl NextTimeWord;	jsr IncTimePtr;*****  NOTE:  the following code is very similar to some code in*****  CheckFLFile,	and can probably be	boiled down into a subroutine*****  usable by both - BHM  9/15/87;NextEntry		;	jsr GetDirEntry	bcc GotEntry;some error:	cmp #EndOfDir	beq NoMoreEntries	;if you call that an error	cmp #1	; was it an invalid call number???	beq NoMoreEntries	; if so, just continue...	sec	;for a real error .	. .	rts;GotEntry		;;the following flip	is to account for the fact that GetDirEntry uses a length;word, while we need it to be a byte (we know the upper byte is 0, anyway);	ldy #(GDENameLen-FMParams)	lda [<FMParamPtr],y	and #$00FF	sta <fNameLen	;useful later	xba	sta [<FMParamPtr],y;now check out that	file;	ldy #(GDEFileType-FMParams)	lda [<FMParamPtr],y	;file type	and #$00FF	;only low byte significant [?]	cmp #FontType	;same as font?	bne NextEntry	;no;yes:	ldy #(GDEAuxType-FMParams)	lda [<FMParamPtr],y	bne NextEntry	;aux type must be 0	iny	iny	lda [<FMParamPtr],y	bne NextEntry	;all of it;it's a font file!;	inc <NumFonts;;copy name into file name list	ldy <fNameLenCopyLoop		;	lda [<fNamePtr],y	sta [<filePtr],y	dey	beq CopyLoop	dey	bpl CopyLoop;	jsr IncFilePtr;;move in the times & dates;	ldy #14NextTimeWord2		;	lda [<fTimePtr],y	sta [<TimePtr],y	dey	dey	bpl NextTimeWord2;	jsr IncTimePtr	brl NextEntry;NoMoreEntries		;;;and this is a good	place to calculate the size of the time	list	lda <TimePtr	sec	sbc <SavedTimePtr	sta <TimeListSize;	jsr UnLockFileList	;unlock filename list	jsr UnlockTimeList	;and time list;and now that it's unlocked, let's shrink the time list	PushWord #0	;high word	lda <TimeListSize	pha	;low	PushZLong <TimeHandle	_SetHandleSize;	clc	rts****************************************	                  **  end GetFileNames	                  **	                  ****************************************;******************************************************************************			                **  subroutine GetListHandles		                **			                **    started 8/27/87		                **    Bennet Marks  x6245		                **			                **  This subroutine gets handles for NameList, FamList, IDList, and          **  FileList.  Each list is allocated a token amount of space (10 bytes).    **  If the subroutine is successful, it returns with carry clear; otherwise  **  it returns with carry set, the error	code in the acc., and none of the   **  handles allocated.  Nice, huh?		                **			                **  GetListHandles returns with an RTS and does not have a separate entry    **  point; it's part of FMStartUp.                                           **			                ******************************************************************************;****************************************	                  **  9/24/87  1:15 pm	                  **  BHM  x6245	                  **	                  ****************************************;GetListHandles		;;	lda #10	;a token amount	jsr GetHandle	bcc GotNameHandle	rtsGotNameHandle		;	sta <NameHandle	stx <NameHandle+2;	lda #10	jsr GetHandle	bcc GotFamHandle	sta errCode	bra HandError1GotFamHandle		;	sta <FamHandle	stx <FamHandle+2;	lda #10	jsr GetHandle	bcc GotIDHandle	sta errCode	bra HandError2GotIDHandle		;	sta <IDHandle	stx <IDHandle+2;	lda #10	jsr GetHandle	bcc GotFileHandle	sta errCode	bra HandError3GotFileHandle		;	sta <FileHandle	stx <FileHandle+2;	lda #10	jsr GetHandle	bcc GotTimeHandle	sta errCode	bra HandError4GotTimeHandle		;	sta <TimeHandle	stx <TimeHandle+2;	clc	rts;HandError4		;	lxy <FileHandle	;8-Mar-93 SS	jsr DisposeTheHandleHandError3		;	lxy <IDHandle	;8-Mar-93 SS	jsr DisposeTheHandleHandError2		;	lxy <FamHandle	;8-Mar-93 SS	jsr DisposeTheHandleHandError1		;	lxy <NameHandle	;8-Mar-93 SS	jsr DisposeTheHandle;	lda errCode	sec	rts****************************************	                  **  end GetListHandles                 **	                  ****************************************;;******************************************************************************			                **  subroutine CloseFONTSDir		                **			                **    started 8/31/87		                **    Bennet Marks  x6245		                **			                **  This subroutine closes the subdirectory *:SYSTEM:FONTS.	If it succeeds, **  it returns with carry clear; otherwise with carry set and the error code **  in the acc.			                **			                **  Currently, CloseFONTSDir returns with an RTS, and does not have a        **  separate entry point; it's just part of FMStartUp.                       **			                ******************************************************************************;****************************************	                  **  9/2/87  1:20 pm	                  **  BHM  x6245	                  **	                  ****************************************;CloseFONTSDir		;;	lda <FONTSDirRef	sta <CloseRef;	jsr CloseFile	rts****************************************	                  **  end CloseFONTSDir                  **	                  ****************************************;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;and some other stuff (here instead of in STDSTUFF;because the time list is local to FMStartUp):;LockTimeList		;;	ldy #4	lda [<TimeHandle],y	ora #$8000	sta [<TimeHandle],y;	lda [<TimeHandle]	sta <TimePtr	ldy #2	lda [<TimeHandle],y	sta <TimePtr+2;	rts;****************;UnlockTimeList		;;	ldy #4	lda [<TimeHandle],y	and #$7FFF	sta [<TimeHandle],y	rts;******************;IncTimePtr		;;	lda <TimePtr	clc	adc #16	sta <TimePtr	lda <TimePtr+2	adc #0	sta <TimePtr+2	rts;                COPY SpeedStuff;******************************************************************************			                **  file SpeedStuff			                **			                **    started 8/24/87		                **    Bennet Marks  x6245		                **			                **  This file contains code which will be integrated into FMStartUp (and     **  possibly other Font Manager calls) to help speed up the Font Manager     **  start-up procedure.  Currently the Font Manager opens every font file    **  in the FONTS subdirectory in order to make lists of available fonts,     **  distinct family names, file names of	font files, etc.  This is very      **  slow.  Our plan is to create a file,	font.lists, that has all that       **  information in it, so that the Font Manager only has to open and read    **  in from that one	file.  The only problem is validation -	how do we know  **  the information in font.lists is still good some time after it was       **  created?  This way:  by remembering the create dates & times and the     **  last-mod dates &	time for every file, we can run a check	on every font   **  file in FONTS to	see if font files with the same names (one as an actual **  file in FONTS, the other as a remembered name & dates & time in          **  font.lists) match.  You would have to go out of your way	to break that   **  validation check.  Also, we will check to see if new font files have     **  shown up, or old	ones disappear.  If	font.lists is good,	we will use the **  info in it.  Otherwise we will go through the long font-reading process, **  and update font.lists while we're at it.                                 **			                **  In our first pass, we'll treat font.lists as either completely valid or  **  utterly useless.	 Later revisions will attempt to integrate new info     **  and discard outdated info, but still	make efficient use of the parts of  **  font.lists that appear to be good.  (In our VERY first pass, we may even **  skip the dates &	times business, and	validate simply on file names; but  **  that's just for demo purposes.)                                          **			                **  Other goals:  making the code ROMable.  Using GetDirEntry instead of     **  reading directory blocks directly.		                **			                ******************************************************************************;******************************************************************************			                **  subroutine FindFileName		                **			                **    started 8/24/87		                **    Bennet Marks  x6245		                **			                **  This subroutine attempts to find a name pointed to by FNamePtr in the    **  list of names pointed to CurrFNamePtr.  If it finds the name, it returns **  with the carry clear, CurrFNamePtr pointing to the matching name in the  **  list, and the "position number" (0-based) of the matching name in the    **  acc.  - 0 if it was the first name, 1 if the second, etc.  If the name   **  isn't found, FindFileName returns with the carry set; CurrFNamePtr and   **  acc. are undefined.		                **			                **  FindFileName also uses numFonts, the	number of file names in the list,   **  but doesn't change it.  (NOTE:  numFonts is a 1-based counter.)          **			                **  All the names are Pascal-type strings (length byte followed by ASCII     **  character codes,	1 per byte).		                **			                **  For now at least, FindFileName returns with an RTS and is not a separate **  entry point; it's just part of FMStartUp.                                **			                ******************************************************************************;***************************************	                  **  9/24/87  2:55 pm	                  **  BHM  x6245	                  **	                  ****************************************;FindFileName;	lda <numFonts	sta <fileCount	;count down;	lda [<fNamePtr]	;length byte	and #$00FF	;and I do mean byte	sta <FNameLen;NextFileName		;	lda [<currFNamePtr]	;length byte	and #$00FF	sta <currFNameLen;	cmp <fNameLen	bne TryNextName	;because the lengths don't match;lengths match - now we compare the names.;we'll go 2 bytes at a time, starting from the last 2 characters:	dec a	tay;NextChars		;	lda [<FNamePtr],y	cmp [<currFNamePtr],y	bne TryNextName	;mismatched characters;	dey	bmi NamesMatch	;(and length was odd - and we;		;rechecked the length byte)	beq NamesMatch	;(and length was even);	dey	bra NextChars;TryNextName		;	dec <fileCount	beq NoSuchName	;no more to try;;advance currFNamePtr:	lda <currFNameLen	inc a	clc	adc <currFNamePtr	sta <currFNamePtr	bcc NoCarry	inc <currFNamePtr+2NoCarry		;	bra NextFileName;NamesMatch		;	lda <numFonts	sec	sbc <fileCount	;to get position in	name list	clc	rts;NoSuchName		;	sec	rts****************************************	                  **  end FindFileName	                  **	                  ****************************************;*******************************************************************************			                 **  subroutine CheckFLFile		                 **			                 **    started 8/24/87		                 **    Bennet Marks  x6245		                 **			                 **  This subroutine checks the "validation" information in FONT.LISTS - file  **  names, create times & dates, and last-mod times & dates - against the     **  corresponding info from the FONTS subdirectory header.  We assume that    **  both the subdirectory and FONT.LISTS	have been opened, with the marks     **  set at their beginnings.  If FONT.LISTS passes the validity test, then    **  CheckFLFile returns with carry clear, and leaves font.lists with the mark **  pointing to the first byte of the recorded ID list.	                 **			                 **  If FONT.LISTS fails the validity test, CheckFLFile returns with the carry **  set; it is then the responsibility of the rest of FMStartUp to construct  **  these lists the old-fashioned (i.e.,	"slow") way, and update FONT.LISTS   **  accordingly.  In	this case FONT.LISTS and FONTS will still be open; FONTS **  will have its mark set to the beginning, and FONT.LISTS will be empty     **  (EOF set to the begining).  Also, the acc. will be 0.  Other errors will  **  signaled by a carry set and acc. not	0.	                 **			                 **  In future versions we will probably get away from this "all-or-nothing"   **  view of FONT.LISTS, and try to use all valid info found in FONT.LISTS,    **  getting the rest	from the font files	themselves.  This will integrate     **  the validating of FONT.LISTS and the	construction of the	Font Manager's   **  lists.  But not now.  Stop nagging.		                 **			                 **  In our earliest passes, we may ignore create & last-mod times & dates,    **  and just check over names - just for	demo purposes.	                 **			                 **  CheckFLFile returns with an RTS and does not have its own entry point.    **  For now it's just part of FMStartUp.                                      **			                 *******************************************************************************;****************************************	                  **  11/10/87  3:35 pm                  **  BHM  x6245	                  **	                  ****************************************;CheckFLFile	lda <FLFileRef	sta <ReadRef	lda #FLFileHeadLen	;for header info in	font.lists	sta <ReadSize***	lda #0***	sta <ReadSize+2	stz <ReadSize+2	;6-Jan-91 DAL	lda <BlockPtr	sta <ReadPtr	lda <BlockPtr+2	sta <ReadPtr+2;(actually, you don't have to do all that, at least not every time -;but I'm just getting used to this stuff - BHM  9/4/87);	jsr ReadFile	bcc ReadIt	rtsReadIt;;check the FONT.LISTS format version number:	lda [<BlockPtr]	cmp #FLVerLo	beq GoodSoFar	brl BadFLFileGoodSoFar	ldy #2	lda [<BlockPtr],y	cmp #FLVerHi	beq VersionGood	brl BadFLFileVersionGood;;compare ROM info to FONT.LISTS' version:	PushZPtr <RomInfoRec	_GetRomFont;	lda <RomFamNum	ldy #oRomFamNum	cmp [<BlockPtr],y	beq RomFamNumOK	brl BadFLFile;RomFamNumOK;	lda <RomStyle	ldy #oRomStyle	cmp [<BlockPtr],y	beq RomStyleOK	brl BadFLFile;RomStyleOK;	lda <RomSize	ldy #oRomSize	cmp [<BlockPtr],y	beq RomSizeOK	brl BadFLFile;RomSizeOK;;(that can actually	be done with a loop, if things are kept	in the right;order);;****  added 10/27/87  (I had forgotten to set SysFontID):;	lda <RomFamNum	sta <SysFontID	lda <RomSize	xba	ora <RomStyle	sta <SysFontID+2;****  end of addition 10/27/87 - BHM x6245;transfer values from FONT.LISTS to FM 0-page:;	ldy #oIDCount	lda [<BlockPtr],y	sta <IDCount	dec a	;for ROM font	sta <numFonts;	ldy #oFamCount	lda [<BlockPtr],y	sta <FamCount;	ldy #oIDListSize	lda [<BlockPtr],y	sta <IDListSize;	ldy #oFamListSize	lda [<BlockPtr],y	sta <FamListSize;	ldy #oNameListSize	lda [<BlockPtr],y	sta <NameListSize;	ldy #oFileListSize	lda [<BlockPtr],y	sta <FileListSize;	ldy #oTimeListSize	lda [<BlockPtr],y	sta <TimeListSize;;;get space for file	list and read it in;	PushWord #0	;high word of size	lda <FileListSize	;low word of size	sta <ReadSize	pha	PushZLong <fileHandle	_SetHandleSize	bcc NoSizeErr1	rtsNoSizeErr1;	jsr LockFileList	lda <FilePtr	sta <ReadPtr	lda <FilePtr+2	sta <ReadPtr+2	lda <FLFileRef	sta <ReadRef***	lda #0***	sta <ReadSize+2	stz <ReadSize+2	;6-Jan-91 DAL;(actually, you don't have to do all that, at least not every time -;but I'm just getting used to this stuff - BHM  9/4/87);	jsr ReadFile	bcc NoReadErr1	sta <errCode	jsr UnlockFileList	lda <errCode	sec	rtsNoReadErr1;;get space for time	list and read it in;	PushWord #0	;high word of size	lda <TimeListSize	;low word of size	sta <ReadSize	pha	PushZLong <TimeHandle	_SetHandleSize	bcc NoSizeErr2	rtsNoSizeErr2;	jsr LockTimeList	lda <TimePtr	sta <ReadPtr	lda <TimePtr+2	sta <ReadPtr+2	lda <FLFileRef	sta <ReadRef***	lda #0***	sta <ReadSize+2	stz <ReadSize+2	;6-Jan-91 DAL;(actually, you don't have to do all that, at least not every time -;but I'm just getting used to this stuff - BHM  9/4/87);	jsr ReadFile	bcc NoReadErr2	sta <errCode	jsr UnlockFileList	jsr UnlockTimeList	lda <errCode	sec	rtsNoReadErr2		;;;now start checking	for validity:;	stz <numFontFiles	lda <FONTSDirRef	ldy #(GDERef-FMParams)	sta [<FMParamPtr],y;NextFilea		;;	jsr GetDirEntry	bcc NoError;some error code:	cmp #EndOfDir	beq NoMoreFiles	sec	;corrected from "clc" - BHM 9/15/87	rtsNoError		;;*****  The following semi-kludge is included because GetDirEntry returns*****  the file name with a length word, rather than a length byte.  Since*****  we know it's <= 16, we can just flip it.;	ldy #(GDENameLen-FMParams)	lda [<FMParamPtr],y	xba	sta [<FMParamPtr],y;*****  Now it's a length byte - BHM  9/9/87;;is it a font file?	ldy #(GDEFileType-FMParams)	lda [<FMParamPtr],y	and #$00FF	;only low byte meaningful	cmp #FontType	bne NextFilea	;wrong type;	ldy #(GDEAuxType-FMParams)	lda [<FMParamPtr],y	bne NextFilea	;AuxType must be 0	iny	iny	lda [<FMParamPtr],y	bne NextFilea	;all of it;;congratulations, it's a font file!	lda <numFontFiles	;seen before now	cmp <numFonts	;from FONT.LISTS	beq BadFLFile	;too many files;	inc <numFontFiles;now try to find this file name;(assume FNamePtr has been set up);	lda <FilePtr	clc	adc #2	;skip dummy entry	sta <currFNamePtr	lda <FilePtr+2	bcc NoCarrya	inc aNoCarrya		;	sta <currFNamePtr+2;	jsr FindFileName	bcc FoundIt	bra BadFLFile	;couldn't find the nameFoundIt		;;;check on dates & times would (will) go	here;and here it is:;position of file name in list of files	is in acc. - now;we want to check out the corresponding	time list entry	inc a	;to skip over ROM font "entry"	asl a	;times 2	asl a	;4	asl a	;8	asl a	;16;	clc	adc <TimePtr	sta <tempPtr	lda <TimePtr+2	adc #0	sta <tempPtr+2;	ldy #14NextTimeWord3		;	lda [<fTimePtr],y	;from GDE call	cmp [<tempPtr],y	;from time list	beq WordMatches	brl BadFLFile	;no it doesn't;WordMatches		;	dey	dey	bpl NextTimeWord3;;all the times & dates matched;	bra NextFilea;NoMoreFiles		;;	lda <numFontFiles	cmp <numFonts	bne BadFLFile;;FONT.LISTS has passed the validity test;hurrah, hurrah!!!;	jsr UnlockFileList	jsr UnlockTimeList	clc	rts;BadFLFile		;;	jsr UnlockFileList	jsr UnlockTimeList;(they may or may not be locked, but so	what?);set FONTS back to its just-opened state, and empty FONT.LISTS:;**** changed to use	0-page parameter block - BHM  x6245  11/4/87:;	lda <FONTSDirRef	sta <MarkRef;	stz <MarkLoc+2	stz <MarkLoc;	jsr SetMark;	lda <FLFileRef	sta <MarkRef;0 position still set;	jsr SetMark;	lda <FLFileRef	sta <EOFRef;;0 position still set;	jsr SetEOF;	lda #0	sec	rts****************************************	                  **  end CheckFLFile	                  **	                  ****************************************;******************************************************************************			                **  subroutine SetUpFMParams		                **			                **    started 8/26/87		                **    Bennet Marks  x6245		                **			                **  This subroutine obtains a block of RAM that the Font Manager can use     **  for parameters that it needs to alter, or may need to alter, such as     **  font file names (for the Open call, for example) and window parameters   **  (which are different in 320 and 640 mode).	                **			                **  When the Font Manager lived in RAM, this information/storage was kept    **  in-line.  We still have the defaults	in-line, but SetUpFMParams copies   **  them over into the RAM space it obtains.	                **			                **  SetUpFMParams has changed so much since its earlier incarnation (when    **  it was mainly used to get ProDOS parameter block space, which is now     **  mainly on 0-page) that we have changed its name from SetUpParams.  Does  **  this make it a born-again subroutine?	                **			                **  If the subroutine succeeds in allocating the space for the parameter     **  blocks, it returns with the carry clear.  Otherwise it returns with the  **  carry set (and the MM error code in the acc.).	                **			                **  As currently written, SetUpParams returns with an RTS and does not have  **  a separate entry	point.  It's just part of FMStartUp.                    **			                ******************************************************************************;****************************************	                  **  11/10/87 3:50 pm	                  **  BHM  x6245	                  **	                  ****************************************;************************************************************		                  **  major re-write, subroutine renamed -	                  **    BHM  x6245  11/10/87	                  **		                  ************************************************************;SetUpFMParams		;;	lda #(EndOfFMParams-FMParams)	jsr GetHandle	bcc GotFMParamMem	rts;GotFMParamMem		;	sta <FMParamHandle	stx <FMParamHandle+2;	jsr LockFMParams;;transfer default values (and a lot of needless zeros):;	lda #FMParams	sta <tempPtr	lda #^FMParams	sta <tempPtr+2*** killing the following--doesn't work if EndOfFMParams-FMParms is odd!;	ldy #(EndOfFMParams-FMParams-2);;;NextParamWord		;;	lda [<tempPtr],y;	sta [<FMParamPtr],y;	dey;	bmi ParamsMoved;	dey;	bra NextParamWord;;;ParamsMoved		;*** 29-Apr-91 DAL -- use BlockMove, the above is trying too hard and is a mess	pei <tempPtr+2	pei <tempPtr	pei <FMParamPtr+2	pei <FMParamPtr	pushlong #EndOfFMParams-FMParams	_BlockMove*** end of 29-Apr-91 DAL;;set up a few needed pointers:;GDE name buffer:	lda <FMParamPtr	clc	adc #(GDENameBuf-FMParams)	sta <tempPtr	ldy #(GDENameBufPtr-FMParams)	sta [<FMParamPtr],y	lda <FMParamPtr+2	bcc NoCarryb	inc aNoCarryb	sta <tempPtr+2	iny	iny	sta [<FMParamPtr],y;;we need easy access to the GDE file name string	lda <tempPtr	clc	adc #3;(that's a 3 to access the length byte we swap into place from;the length word provided by GetDirEntry)	sta <fNamePtr	lda <tempPtr+2	bcc NoCarryc	inc aNoCarryc	sta <fNamePtr+2;;we also need a pointer to the times & dates within the GetDirEntry block:	lda <FMParamPtr	clc	adc #(GDECreateTime-FMParams)	sta <fTimePtr	lda <FMParamPtr+2	bcc NoCarryd	inc a	clcNoCarryd	sta <fTimePtr+2;	rts****************************************	                  **  end of SetUpParams                 **	                  ****************************************;************************************************************************ Subroutine KillBadFLFile** 11/13/89 Mensch* Added this routine so that the Font,list file could be killed if it* were bad. This is usually caused by a failure to complete the write. So* this routine is called when the write fails...* * This routine closes/destroys file file Font.Lists and then resets ths file* number to zero internally*	import DestroyFile***********************************************************************KillBadFLFile;; First close the file so that it can be destroyed...	jsr CloseFLFile; Coppied this pre-amble from open file...;	lda <FMParamPtr	clc	adc #(FLFileName-FMParams)	sta <FilePtr	lda <FMParamPtr+2	adc #0	sta <FilePtr+2;	jsr CopyFileName;	lda <FMParamPtr	clc	adc #(DirName-FMParams)	sta <KillNamePtr	lda <FMParamPtr+2	adc #0	sta <KillNamePtr+2;	jsr DestroyFile	; now call destroy...	rts	; and exit the hell outta here...******************************************************************************			                **  subroutine OpenFLFile		                **			                **    started 8/28/87		                **    Bennet Marks  x6245		                **			                **  This subroutine finds and opens font.lists, if it can.  It has 3 poss-   **  ible outcomes:  (1)  carry clear:  font.lists found and opened.          **  (2)  carry set, acc. 0:  font.lists not found, so OpenFLFile created     **  and then opened it.  (3)  carry set,	acc. not 0:  some other error       **  occurred during the attempted to open it.	                **			                **  OpenFLFile returns with an RTS, and does not have a separate entry       **  point; it's a part of FMStartUp.                                         **			                ******************************************************************************;****************************************	                  **  11/12/87  1:50 pm                  **  BHM  x6245	                  **	                  ****************************************;OpenFLFile;****  changed to use FMParams block - BHM  x6245  11/12/87;	lda <FMParamPtr	clc	adc #(FLFileName-FMParams)	sta <FilePtr	lda <FMParamPtr+2	adc #0	sta <FilePtr+2;	jsr CopyFileName;	lda <FMParamPtr	clc	adc #(DirName-FMParams)	sta <OpenPtr	lda <FMParamPtr+2	adc #0	sta <OpenPtr+2;	jsr OpenFile	bcc GotFLFilea;some error:	cmp #FileNotFound	beq CreateFLFile;real error:	sec	rts;GotFLFilea	lda <OpenRef	sta <FLFileRef	clc	rts;CreateFLFile	lda <FMParamPtr	clc	adc #(DirName-FMParams);(still set to FONT.LISTS)	sta <CRNamePtr	lda <FMParamPtr+2	adc #0	sta <CRNamePtr+2;	lda #$C3	;access word	sta <CRAccess;	lda #BinFile	;file type;	sta <CRFileType;	lda #0;	sta <CRAuxType	;aux type;	sta <CRAuxType+2	;and more aux type*** 30-Sep-91 DAL -- use filetype $5A;0008 for Font.Lists file	lda #$005A	;config file	sta <CRFileType	lda #$0008	sta <CRAuxType	stz <CRAuxType+2*** end 30-Sep-91 DAL	stz <CRDate	;0 means ProDOS will fill in date	stz <CRTime	;and time	lda #$01	;storage type	sta <CRStore	jsr CreateFile	bcc MadeFLFile; some error:	rtsMadeFLFile;now open it;(the name is still	set from earlier in	the routine)	lda <FMParamPtr	clc	adc #(DirName-FMParams);(we should probably be saving this pointer rether than recalculating;it every time.  Maybe.)	sta <OpenPtr	lda <FMParamPtr+2	adc #0	sta <OpenPtr+2;	jsr OpenFile	bcc FLFileNowOpen;bad craziness:	rts;FLFileNowOpen	lda <OpenRef	sta <FLFileRef	lda #0	sec	rts****************************************	                  **  end OpenFLFile	                  **	                  ****************************************;******************************************************************************			                **  subroutine ReadFontLists		                **			                **    started 8/31/87		                **    Bennet Marks  x6245		                **			                **  This subroutine reads in the ID list, the fam list, and the name list    **  from FONT.LISTS into the Font Manager's internal lists.  We assume that  **  FONT.LISTS has passed the validity test, and its mark is	now pointing at **  the start of its	copy of the ID list.  If ReadFontLists succeeds, it     **  returns with the	carry clear; otherwise it returns with the carry set    **  and the error code in the acc.  (The	possible errors are	in file-reading **  and handle-sizing.)		                **			                **  ReadFontLists returns with an RTS and doesn't have its own entry point;  **  it's part of FMStartUp.                                                  **			                ******************************************************************************;****************************************	                  **  9/11/87  3:00 pm	                  **  BHM  x6245	                  **	                  ****************************************;ReadFontLists		;;	PushWord #0	;high word of size*	lda <IDListSize	;low word of size*	pha	pei <IDListSize	PushZLong <IDHandle	_SetHandleSize	bcc NoSizeErr1a	rtsNoSizeErr1a		;;	PushWord #0	;high word of size*	lda <FamListSize	;low word of size*	pha	pei <FamListSize	PushZLong <FamHandle	_SetHandleSize	bcc NoSizeErr2a	rtsNoSizeErr2a		;;	PushWord #0	;high word of size*	lda <NameListSize	;low word of size*	pha	pei <NameListSize	PushZLong <NameHandle ;(*corrected 9/11/87 - BHM*)	_SetHandleSize	bcc NoSizeErr3	rtsNoSizeErr3		;;	jsr LockIdList	jsr LockFamList	jsr LockNameList;	lda <FLFileRef	sta <ReadRef;	lda <IDPtr	sta <ReadPtr	lda <IDPtr+2	sta <ReadPtr+2	stz <ReadSize+2	;high word of size	lda <IDListSize	;low word	sta <ReadSize	jsr ReadFile	bcs FileReadError;	lda <FamPtr	sta <ReadPtr	lda <FamPtr+2	sta <ReadPtr+2	lda <FamListSize	sta <ReadSize;(high word of ReadSize is already 0)	jsr ReadFile	bcs FileReadError;	lda <NamePtr	sta <ReadPtr; WHOA people, this next line was this:;	lda <FamPtr+2; This seems to be incorrect (to say the least...) we will now change it to correctly use the; proper namePtr and this should fix a rather elusive bug that only sprung up with; stylewares stuff! imagine the shame on our faces! this should teach use a cut amnd paste lesson!	lda <NamePtr+2	; 3/24/89 Mensch	sta <ReadPtr+2	lda <NameListSize	sta <ReadSize;(high word of ReadSize is already 0)	jsr ReadFile	bcs FileReadError;;replace the ROM font handle read in from the FONT.LISTS ID	list with the;guaranteed one obtained from GetROMFont:	lda <ROMFontHndl	ldy #10	sta [<IDPtr],y	lda <ROMFontHndl+2	iny	iny	sta [<IDPtr],y;	jsr UnlockIDList	jsr UnlockFamList	jsr UnlockNameList	clc	rts;FileReadError		;	rts****************************************	                  **  end of ReadFontLists               **	                  ****************************************;******************************************************************************			                **  subroutine CloseFLFile		                **			                **    started 8/31/87		                **    Bennet Marks  x6245		                **			                **  This subroutine closes the file FONT.LISTS.  If it succeeds, it returns  **  with carry clear; otherwise with carry set and the error	code in the     **  acc.			                **			                **  CloseFLFile returns with an RTS, and	does not have its own entry point;  **  it's just part of FMStartUp.                                             **			                ******************************************************************************;****************************************	                  **  8/31/87  2:30 pm	                  **  BHM  x6245	                  **	                  ****************************************;CloseFLFile		;;	lda <FLFileRef	sta <CloseRef	beq @NoFileToCLose;	jsr CloseFile	bcs @ooooops	stz <FLFileRef@ooooops	rts@NoFileToClose	clc;	rts****************************************	                  **  end of CloseFLFile                 **	                  ****************************************;******************************************************************************			                **  subroutine UpdateFLFile		                **			                **    started 8/31/87		                **    Bennet Marks			                **			                **  This subroutine writes out to the file FONTS.LISTS the values and lists  **  that the FM has put together from all the fonts in FONTS	- this is done  **  when FONT.LISTS doesn't pass the validity test.  We assume FONT.LISTS    **  exists, is open,	and is empty - earlier routines have arranged this.     **			                **  If UpdateFLFile is successful, it returns with carry clear; otherwise it **  returns with carry set and the error	code in the acc.  The subroutine    **  returns with an RTS, and doesn't have its own entry point; it's part of  **  FMStartUp.			                **			                ******************************************************************************;****************************************	                  **  11/7/87  2:00 pm	                  **  BHM  x6245	                  **	                  ****************************************;UpdateFLFile		;;	lda #FLVerLo	sta [<BlockPtr]	lda #FLVerHi	ldy #2	sta [<BlockPtr],y;	lda <RomFamNum	ldy #oRomFamNum	sta [<BlockPtr],y;	lda <RomStyle	ldy #oRomStyle	sta [<BlockPtr],y;	lda <RomSize	ldy #oRomSize	sta [<BlockPtr],y;	lda <IDCount	ldy #oIDCount	sta [<BlockPtr],y;	lda <FamCount	ldy #oFamCount	sta [<BlockPtr],y;	lda <IDListSize	ldy #oIDListSize	sta [<BlockPtr],y;	lda <FamListSize	ldy #oFamListSize	sta [<BlockPtr],y;	lda <NameListSize	ldy #oNameListSize	sta [<BlockPtr],y;	lda <FileListSize	ldy #oFileListSize	sta [<BlockPtr],y;	lda <TimeListSize	ldy #oTimeListSize	sta [<BlockPtr],y;	lda <FLFileRef	sta <WriteRef	stz <WriteReq+2	;high word of request	lda #FLFileHeadLen	;low word	sta <WriteReq	lda <BlockPtr	sta <WriteBuf	lda <BlockPtr+2	sta <WriteBuf+2;	jsr WriteFile	bcc WroteHeader	rtsWroteHeader		;;	lda <FileListSize	sta <WriteReq;(high word still 0);high word is 0 and	stays 0	lda <SavedFilePtr	sta <WriteBuf	lda <SavedFilePtr+2	sta <WriteBuf+2;	jsr WriteFile	bcc WroteFileList	rtsWroteFileList		;;	lda <TimeListSize	sta <WriteReq;(high word still 0)	lda <SavedTimePtr	sta <WriteBuf	lda <SavedTimePtr+2	sta <WriteBuf+2;	jsr WriteFile	bcc WroteTimeList	rtsWroteTimeList		;;	lda <IDListSize	sta <WriteReq;(high word still 0)	lda <SavedIDPtr	sta <WriteBuf	lda <SavedIDPtr+2	sta <WriteBuf+2;	jsr WriteFile	bcc WroteIDList	rtsWroteIDList		;;	lda <FamListSize	sta <WriteReq;(oh, you know!)	lda <SavedFamPtr	sta <WriteBuf	lda <SavedFamPtr+2	sta <WriteBuf+2;	jsr WriteFile	bcc WroteFamList	rtsWroteFamList		;;	lda <NameListSize	sta <WriteReq	lda <SavedNamePtr	sta <WriteBuf	lda <SavedNamePtr+2	sta <WriteBuf+2;	jsr WriteFile;(SURELY that can be looped!);(yes, it probably can - and don't call me Shirley . . .);	rts****************************************	                  **  end UpdateFLFile	                  **	                  ****************************************;;	ENDP****************************************************************** FMShutDown*****************************************************************	ENTRY FMShutDownFMShutDown	PROCCount	equ Temp	phd	tcd	bne Doit	ldx #ActiveErr	;return error if Font Mgr not active	ldy #0	;param size	jml errout;set QuickDraw system font to ROM fontDoit	jsr LockIDList	;ROM font is first entry in list	ldy #12	lda [<IDPtr],y	;push handle to ROM	font	pha	dey	dey	lda [<IDPtr],y	pha	_SetSysFont	;set QuickDraw system font to ROM font;dispose of all fonts in memory, except	application-generated fonts	stz <Count	bra NextID	;skip ROM fontLoop	jsr CheckHandle	beq NextID	;branch if no handle to font	PushWord #3	;in case it's an app font	PushzLong <FontHandle ;push handle to font on stack	ldy #8	lda [<IDPtr],y	;get info word	and #ApVarBit	;is this an application generated font?	bne AppFont	;yes - so don't dispose of handle	_DisposeHandle	;no - so dispose of	font and handle	pla	;clean up stack	bra NextIDAppFont	_SetPurge	;make font purgeableNextID	jsr IncIDPtr	inc <Count	lda <Count	cmp <IDCount	;at end of list?	bne Loop	;no	jsr UnLockIDList;dispose of the data lists	lxy <FileHandle	;8-Mar-93 SS	jsr DisposeTheHandle	;release filename list space	lxy <IDHandle	;8-Mar-93 SS	jsr DisposeTheHandle	;release ID list space	lxy <FamHandle	;8-Mar-93 SS	jsr DisposeTheHandle	;release family list space	lxy <NameHandle	;8-Mar-93 SS	jsr DisposeTheHandle	;release famname list space;	lxy <FMParamHandle ;and the paramter space	jsr DisposeTheHandle	;8-Mar-93 SS	lda <MenuMade	;was an Item list created?	beq NoItemList	;no	lxy <ItemHandle ;yes - so release	the space	jsr DisposeTheHandle	;8-Mar-93 SSNoItemList		;;clear work area pointer	PushWord #0	PushWord #FMTSNum	PushWord #0	PushWord #0	_SetWAP	;clear work area pointer	ldy #0	;param size	jml endcall	ENDP****************************************************************** FMVersion*****************************************************************	ENTRY FMVersionFMVersion	PROC	lda #FMVerNum	sta 7,s	brl oStdEnd0	ENDP****************************************************************** FMReset*****************************************************************	ENTRY FMResetFMReset	PROC	cmp #0	;is FM active?	beq Done	;no	ldx #ResetErr	;yes - so return error	ldy #0	;param size	jml oerroutDone	brl oStdEnd0	ENDP****************************************************************** FMStatus*****************************************************************	ENTRY FMStatusFMStatus	PROC	sta 7,s	brl oStdEnd0	ENDP;;;;;;                COPY famstuff****************************************************************** CountFamilies*****************************************************************	ENTRY CountFamiliesCountFamilies	PROCBaseCount	equ Temp	phd	tcd	lda 9,s	;get spec bits	and #BaseOnlyBit	;only count Base families?	beq CountAll	;no	jsr LockFamList	;yes	ldy #4	;index to info word	in fam entry	ldx #0	;# of fam entries processed	stz <BaseCount	;# base families foundLoop	lda [<FamPtr],y	;get info word	and #NotBaseBit	bne NextFam	;branch if not a Base family	inc <BaseCountNextFam	jsr IncFamPtr	inx	cpx <FamCount	;at end of fam list?	bne Loop	;no	jsr UnLockFamList	lda <BaseCount	;return # of Base families	bra DoneCountAll	lda <FamCount	;get total # of fam	entriesDone	sta 11,s	ldy #2	;param size	jml endcall	ENDP****************************************************************** FindFamily*****************************************************************	ENTRY FindFamilyFindFamily	PROCBaseCount	equ TempMult2	equ BaseCount+2	phd	tcd	jsr LockFamList	lda 15,s	;get spec bits	and #BaseOnlyBit	;Base families only?	bne CheckBase	;yes	lda 13,s	;get position num	dec a	cmp <FamCount	;valid number?	bcs NoFam	;no	asl a	;multiply by 6 to get offset to correct	sta <Mult2	;fam entry	asl a	clc	adc <Mult2	clc	adc <FamPtr	;create ptr to fam entry	sta <FamPtr	lda <FamPtr+2	adc #0	sta <FamPtr+2	bra GotFamCheckBase	ldx #0	;# of fam entries processed	stz <BaseCount	;# of Base families	processed	ldy #4	;index to info word	in fam entryLoop	lda [<FamPtr],y	;get info word	and #NotBaseBit	bne NextFam	;not a Base fam - so don't count fam	inc <BaseCount	lda <BaseCount	cmp 13,s	;correct fam entry?	beq GotFam	;yesNextFam	jsr IncFamPtr	inx	cpx <FamCount	;at end of fam list?	bne Loop	;noNoFam	lda #Illegal	;didn't find family	sta 17,s	;return illegal fam	num	bra DoneGotFam	lda [<FamPtr]	;get fam #	sta 17,s	;and return it	lda 9,s	;get ptr to output string	sta <TempPtr	ora 11,s	;is ptr all zeros?	beq Done	;yes - so don't return name	lda 11,s	sta <TempPtr+2	jsr LockNameList	ldy #2	lda [<FamPtr],y	;get offset to famname entry	clc	adc <NamePtr	;create ptr to famname entry	sta <NamePtr	lda <NamePtr+2	adc #0	sta <NamePtr+2	lda [<NamePtr]	;get name length	and #$00FF	;mask off hi byte	tay	deyCopyLoop	lda [<NamePtr],y	;copy famname into output string	sta [<TempPtr],y	dey	beq CopyLoop	dey	bpl CopyLoop	jsr UnLockNameListDone	jsr UnLockFamList	ldy #8	;param size	jml endcall	ENDP****************************************************************** GetFamInfo*****************************************************************	ENTRY GetFamInfoGetFamInfo	PROC	phd	tcd	lda 13,s	;get fam #	tay	lda #$0100	;fake style/size	jsr CheckFontID	bcc IDOK	brl StdErr6	;return errorIDOK	tya	sta 13,s	;save converted fam	#	jsr LockFamList	ldx #0	;# of fam entries checkedFamLoop	lda [<FamPtr]	;get fam #	cmp 13,s	;match?	beq GotFam	;yes	jsr IncFamPtr	inx	cpx <FamCount	;have we checked all fam entries?	bne FamLoop	;no	lda #NotFoundBit	;yes - so the fam doesn't exist	sta 15,s	;return 'NotFound'	brl DoneGotFam	ldy #4	lda [<FamPtr],y	;get info word	sta 15,s	;and return it	lda 9,s	;get ptr to output string	sta <TempPtr	ora 11,s	;is ptr 0?	beq Done	;yes - so don't return famname	lda 11,s	sta <TempPtr+2	jsr LockNameList	ldy #2	clc	lda <NamePtr	;get ptr to start of famname list and	adc [<FamPtr],y	;add famname offset	to create	sta <NamePtr	;ptr to correct famname	lda <NamePtr+2	adc #0	sta <NamePtr+2	lda [<NamePtr]	;get name length	and #$00FF	;mask off hi byte	tay	deyLoop	lda [<NamePtr],y	;copy famname into output string	sta [<TempPtr],y	dey	beq Loop	dey	bpl Loop	jsr UnLockNameListDone	jsr UnLockFamList	brl StdEnd6	ENDP****************************************************************** GetFamNum*****************************************************************	ENTRY GetFamNumGetFamNum	PROCMult2	equ TempFirstWord	equ Mult2+2	phd	tcd	lda 9,s	;get ptr to famname	sta <TempPtr	lda 11,s	sta <TempPtr+2	lda [<TempPtr]	;get first 2 bytes of name	sta <FirstWord	;and save	and #$00FF	;get name length	bne NotZero	ldx #NameErr	;name length is 0	brl StdErr4	;return errorNotZero	cmp #MaxNameLen+1	;check length of name	bcc LenOK	lda <FirstWord	;too long - so truncate	and #$FF00	;get saved first 2 bytes and set	ora #MaxNameLen	;length byte to max	name length	sta <FirstWord	;and saveLenOK	jsr LockNameList	ldx #0	;# of famname entries checkedNameLoop	lda [<NamePtr]	;do the first 2 bytes of this famname	cmp <FirstWord	;entry match the input name?	bne NextName	;no - so go on to next name;		;yes - so compare the rest of the name	and #$00FF	;mask off hi byte to get name length	tay	deyCmpLoop	beq Match	;already compared first word so match	lda [<NamePtr],y	;compare names	cmp [<TempPtr],y	bne NextName	;branch if no match	dey	dey	bpl CmpLoop;		;the name matches exactlyMatch	phx	;save index to name	jsr LockFamList	pla	;get index to name and multiply by 6	asl a	sta <Mult2	asl a	clc	adc <Mult2	tay	;to get offset into	fam list	lda [<FamPtr],y	;get fam # from fam	entry	sta 13,s	;and return it	jsr UnLockFamList	bra DoneNextName	jsr IncNamePtr	inx	cpx <FamCount	;done with list?	bne NameLoop	;no - so continue	lda #Illegal	;yes - so no match	sta 13,s	;return illegal fam	#Done	jsr UnLockNameList	brl StdEnd4	ENDP****************************************************************** AddFamily*****************************************************************	ENTRY AddFamilyAddFamily	PROCNewFamSize	equ TempNewNameSize	equ NewFamSize+2	phd	tcd	lda 13,s	;get fam #	beq NumErr	;error if 0	cmp #Illegal	;illegal # ?	bne NumOK	;noNumErr	ldx #FamNumErr	brl StdErr6	;return errorNumOK	lda 9,s	;get ptr to new family name	sta <TempPtr	lda 11,s	sta <TempPtr+2	lda [<TempPtr]	and #$00FF	;get name length	bne NotZero	ldx #NameErr	;name length is 0	brl StdErr6	;return errorNotZero	clc	lda <FamListSize	;get size of family	list	adc #6	;add size of new entry	sta <NewFamSize	;and save	PushWord #0	;hi word of size	pha	;lo word of size	PushZLong <FamHandle ;handle to list	_SetHandleSize	;grow the list	bcc OK	tax	;error code	brl StdErr6	;return errorOK	lda [<TempPtr]	;get length of name	and #$00FF	;mask off hi byte	cmp #MaxNameLen+1	;check length of fam name	bcc LenOK	lda #MaxNameLen	;too long - so truncate nameLenOK	inc a	;add 1 for length byte itself	clc	adc <NameListSize	;add size of new entry to current size	sta <NewNameSize	;and save	PushWord #0	;hi word of size	pha	;lo word of size	PushZLong <NameHandle ;handle to list	_SetHandleSize	;grow the list	bcc OK2	pha	;save error code	PushWord #0	;hi word of size	PushZWord <FamListSize ;lo word of size	PushZLong <FamHandle ;handle to list	_SetHandleSize	;shrink fam list back to previous size	plx	;retrieve error code	brl StdErr6	;return errorOK2	jsr LockFamList	jsr LockNameList	clc	lda <FamPtr	adc <FamListSize	;create ptr to new fam entry	sta <FamPtr	lda <FamPtr+2	adc #0	sta <FamPtr+2	clc	lda <NamePtr	adc <NameListSize	;create ptr to new famname entry	sta <NamePtr	lda <NamePtr+2	adc #0	sta <NamePtr+2	lda 13,s	;get fam #	sta [<FamPtr]	;and store in new fam entry	ldy #2	lda <NameListSize	;get offset to new famname entry	sta [<FamPtr],y	;and store in new fam entry	iny	iny	lda #ApFamBit	ora #NotBaseBit	sta [<FamPtr],y	;set info word	jsr CopyFamName	;copy famname into new famname entry	jsr UnLockNameList	jsr UnLockFamList	lda <NewFamSize	;get new size of fam list	sta <FamListSize	;and save	lda <NewNameSize	;get new size of name list	sta <NameListSize	;and save	inc <FamCount	;inc family count	brl StdEnd6	ENDP********************************************************************************NewInstallWithStats	PROC** Description:	This is a new install font call that will be patched to get rid*	of the orphan problem*** Inputs:	None** Outputs:	None** External Refs:** Entry Points:********************************************************************************FMDPage	equ 1oldDPage	equ FMDPage+2theRTLs	equ oldDPage+2resultPtr	equ theRTLs+6scaleWord	equ resultPtr+4desiredID	equ scaleWord+2;; Set up the stack for the new call...	phd	; save the current DPage	pha	; save the FMDPage	tsc	; get the stack pointer and make it	tcd	; the current pdage	lda #0	; zero our flag	sta >KludgeFlag; set up the parms for the call@CallItAgainSam	pei desiredID+2	pei desiredID	pei ScaleWord	pei ResultPtr+2	pei ResultPtr	jsl xInstallStat	; call the real install font	tax	bcc @skipKludge	; test if an error occured	lda >KludgeFlag	; see if this is the second time thru	bne @SkipKludge	dec a	; if not set the second time thru flag and	sta >KludgeFlag	; try it again!	bra @CallItAgainSam	; and try it one more time...@SkipKludge	txa	pld	; get the FMDPage back again	pld	; get the apps dpage back...	tay	; save the error code in <Y>	lda 1,s	; move the RTL's down 10 bytes	sta 11,s	lda 3,s	sta 13,s	lda 5,s	sta 15,s	pla	; discard 10 bytes of parms	pla	pla	pla	pla	tya	; place error back into <A>	cmp #1	; set error flag properly	rtl	; and end...xInstallStat	lda <FMDPage	; font manager dpage in <A>	jsl InstallWithStats	; call the real install font	rtl	ENTRY KludgeFlagKludgeFlag	ds.W 1	EndP		EJECT********************************************************************************NewInstallFont	PROC** Description:	This is a new install font call that will be patched to get rid*	of the orphan problem*** Inputs:	None** Outputs:	None** External Refs:** Entry Points:********************************************************************************FMDPage	equ 1oldDPage	equ FMDPage+2theRTLs	equ oldDPage+2scaleWord	equ theRTLs+6desiredID	equ scaleWord+2;; Set up the stack for the new call...	phd	; save the current DPage	pha	; save the FMDPage	tsc	; get the stack pointer and make it	tcd	; the current pdage	lda #0	; init flag so only retry once.	sta >KludgeFlag@CallItAgainSam; set up the parms for the call	pei desiredID+2	pei desiredID	pei ScaleWord	jsl xInstallFont	; call the real install font	tax	bcc @skipKludge	; test if an error occured	lda >KludgeFlag	; see if this is the second time thru	bne @SkipKludge	dec a	; if not set the second time thru flag and	sta >KludgeFlag	; try it again!	bra @CallItAgainSam	; and try it one more time...@SkipKludge	txa	pld	; get the FMDPage back again	pld	; get the apps dpage back...	tay	; save the error code in <Y>	lda 1,s	; move the RTL's down 6 bytes	sta 7,s	lda 3,s	sta 9,s	lda 5,s	sta 11,s	pla	; discard 6 bytes of parms	pla	pla	tya	; place error back into <A>	cmp #1	; set error flag properly	rtl	; and end...xInstallFont	lda <FMDPage	; font manager dpage in <A>	jsl InstallFont	; call the real install font	rtl	EndP	****************************************************************** InstallFont*****************************************************************;****************************************	                  **  Sept. 18, 1987  10:30 am           **	                  ****************************************;*****************************************************************  font scaling added**    Bennet Marks  x6245  2/10/87**  changes made to get the right incarnation of the system*  font (that is, right size and style)	in the no-such-family*  case**    Bennet Marks  x6245  3/31/87******************************************************************InstallFont	PROC	INCLUDE 'SomeFMEqus' ;added 2/12/87 - BHM	phd	tcd		stz <Err	;clear error flag	lda 11,s	;get fam #	tay	lda 13,s	;get style/size	jsr CheckFontID	bcc IDOK	brl StdErr6	;return errorIDOK	sta 13,s	;save converted style/size;	and #$00FF	sta <WantStyle	lda 13,s	and #$FF00	sta <WantSize;	tya	sta 11,s	;save converted fam	#	sta <WantFam;TryAgain;	jsr LockIDList;****  temporary fix	to get IDList out of a jam;**  Drop this for now - BHM  9/17/87;              jsr UnlockIDList;****  end of temporary fix - BHM  2/12/87;;	jsr FindBestFit	;find font which best fits request	bcs LoadSys	;system font is best fit;****  quick fix added for byte-switch problems - BHM  2/11/87;	lda <WantSize	xba	sta <WantSize;	lda <BestSize	xba	sta <BestSize;****  end of quick fix;********    FONT SCALING ADDITIONS:;	lda <BestSize	cmp <WantSize	beq DontScale;	lda 9,s	;scaleWord	and #dontScaleBit	bne DontScale;scale:	lda #currFlag	jsr LoadTheFont	;get the best fit font;*****************************************************************  NOTE:  we count on the fact that there are no memory*  manager calls that could get the loaded-in font purged*  (in the case where it is purgeable) between here and*  the call to ScaleFont.  If you make any changes -*  watch it!**  BHM 6/15/87****************************************************************;	bcc GotFont	;got it;error:	lda <Err;if we've already got an error (which means this is not our first;pass), keep the old error code	bne GotErr1	stx <Err	;o.w. save itGotErr1		;	bra LoadSys;GotFont		;;put important values where ScaleFont expects them:	ldx <bestSize	ldy <wantSize	lda <progID;	jsl ScaleFont	bcc ItsScaled;error:	ldx <Err	bne GotErr2	;save old error code, if there is one	sta <Err	;o.w. keep this oneGotErr2		;	bra LoadSys;ItsScaled		;** Add this for now	- experimental - BHM  9/17/87	sta <tempPtr	;font handle low word from ScaleFont** (just trust me on that one, folks)	ldy #4	lda [<BestPtr],y	;offset to fam name	sta <matchLevel	;temp. storage	ldy #8	lda [<BestPtr],y	;font stat bits	sta <newLevel	;temp. storage;****  the following	added for FontForADay call - experimental;;the font was scaled, which means it didn't exist in the first place,;so we return an "oldStats" value with notFoundBit = 1 - and, in;theory, the rest undefined.  Out of politeness, though, we'll use put;in some reasonable	values for the other bits.;	ora #(notFoundBit+notDiskBit+purgeBit+unrealBit)	and #(notMemBit);apFamBit and apVarBit inherited from original	sta <oldStats;****  end of experimental FontForADay additions - BHM  x6245  12/16/87	lda <tempPtr;	jsl AddScaledFont	;add it to lists, make it current	bcc OK	ldx <Err	bne GotErr3	;save old error code	sta <Err	;if none, save new oneGotErr3	bra LoadSys;DontScale;just install best fit:	lda #$FFFF	jsr LoadTheFont	bcc OK;*;;; Changed from ldx 5/6/87 - BHM: 	lda <Err	;old error?	bne GotErr4	;then save it*;;; Changed from sta 5/6/87 - BHM: 	stx <Err	;o.w. save new error code;GotErr4		;on error, fall into . . .;****  END OF ADDITIONS - BHM  2/10/87;LoadSys;yeah, but which one?;	lda WantFam	cmp <SysFontID	;current system font family number	bne TrySysFontFam;WantFam is already	system font family:;	lda <SysFontID+2	and #$00FF	;system font style	eor #$FFFF	ora WantStyle	cmp #$FFFF	beq GoodSysStyle;but the system font style does not partially match WantStyle -;so force it to:	lda <SysFontID+2	and #$00FF	ora WantStyle	sta WantStyle	lda 13,s	and #$FF00	sta <WantSize	;restored from possible xba	brl TryAgain;TrySysFontFam;no good WantFam font around - shift to	system font family:	lda <SysFontID	sta WantFam	lda 13,s	and #$FF00	sta <WantSize	;restored from possible xba	brl TryAgain;GoodSysStyle;WantFam is SysFontFam, and SysFontStyle partially matches WantStyle -;I have no idea what's the matter, so let's do the simplist	thing:;	jsl xLoadSysFont	;make system font currentOK	lda 13,s	;get the requested font ID	pha	lda 13,s	pha	_SetFontID	;set the FontID field in the GrafPort	lda 13,s	and #$00FF	;get the requested font style	pha	_SetTextFace	;set text face field in the GrafPort	lda 13,s	and #$FF00	;get the requested font size	xba	pha	_SetTextSize	;set the text size field in the GrafPort	jsr UnLockIDList	ldx <Err	;get error flag	beq NoErr	brl StdErr6	;report the errorNoErr	brl StdEnd6xLoadSysFont	tdc	jsl LoadSysFont	rtl;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------FindBestFit		;;	stz <Count	;# of ID entries processed	stz <MatchLevel	;size match level	stz <BestStyle	;style byte of best	fit so far	stz <BestSize	;size byte of best fit so far	stz <BestPtr	;ptr to ID entry of	best fit so far	stz <BestPtr+2IDLoop	lda [<IDPtr]	;get fam #	cmp WantFam	;match desired fam #?	beq FamMatch	;yes	brl NextID	;noFamMatch	ldy #2	lda [<IDPtr],y	and #$00FF	;get style byte	sta <IDStyle	;and save	lda <IDStyle	;is this font's style a subset of	ora <WantStyle	;the desired style ?	cmp <WantStyle	beq StyleMatch	;yes	brl NextID	;noStyleMatch	lda [<IDPtr],y	and #$FF00	;get size byte	sta <IDSize	;and save	lda <IDSize	cmp <WantSize	;does font's size match desired size?	bne WrongSize	;no	ldx #5	;yes - so new match	level is 5	bra ContWrongSize	lda <MatchLevel	;have we found correct size yet?	cmp #5	bne NoSizeMatch	;no	brl NextID	;yesNoSizeMatch	ldy #8	lda [<IDPtr],y	;get info word	and #UnrealBit	;is font real?	beq CheckTwice	;yes - so it's OK	brl NextID	;no - so no goodCheckTwice	lda <IDSize	lsr a	;divide font's size by 2	bit #$0080	bne CheckHalf	;doesn't count if not an even size	cmp <WantSize	;is font's size twice as big as desired?	bne CheckHalf	;no	ldx #4	;yes - so new match	level is 4	bra ContCheckHalf	lda <IDSize	asl a	;multiply font's size by 2	cmp <WantSize	;is font's size half as big as desired?	bne CheckBigger	;no	ldx #3	;yes - so new match	level is 3	bra ContCheckBigger	lda <IDSize	cmp <WantSize	;is font's size > desired size?	bcc CheckSmaller	;no	ldx #2	;yes - so new match	level is 2	cpx <MatchLevel	;is current match level = 2 ?	bne Cont	;no	lda <IDSize	;yes	cmp <BestSize	;is font's size < best size so far ?	bcc SaveIt	;yes - so it's a better match	brl NextID	;no - so no goodCheckSmaller	ldx #1	;new match level is	1	cpx <MatchLevel	;is current match level = 1 ?	bne Cont	;no	lda <IDSize	;yes	cmp <BestSize	;is font's size > best size so far ?	bcs SaveIt	;yes - so it's a better match	bra NextID	;no - so no goodCont	stx <NewLevel	;save new match level	ldy #8	lda [<IDPtr],y	;get info word	and #NotDiskBit	;is font on disk?	beq CmpLevels	;yes	jsr CheckHandle	;no - so check handle	beq NextID	;handle is nil - so	font was purgedCmpLevels	ldx <NewLevel	;get new match level and	cpx <MatchLevel	;compare it to best	match level so far	beq SizeTie	;same  - so compare	styles	bcc NextID	;smaller so no good	stx <MatchLevel	;save new match level as best match	bra SaveIt	;save this font as best so far;this font has same	size as 'best so far', so compare their	stylesSizeTie	lda <BestStyle	jsr CountStyles	;count # of styles set in best so far	sta <NumStyles	;and save	lda <IDStyle	jsr CountStyles	;count # of styles set in this font	cmp <NumStyles	;compare with # for	best so far	beq StyleTie	;both fonts have same # styles set	bcs SaveIt	;this font has more	styles set than best	bra NextID	;this font has less	styles set than best;this font has same	# of styles as 'best so far', so see if	it's in memoryStyleTie	jsr CheckHandle	;do we have a handle to this font?	beq NextID	;no	jsr CheckNil	;yes - so check handle	beq NextID	;handle is nil - so	font was purged;this font is best so farSaveIt	ldy #2	lda [<IDPtr],y	;get style/size word	cmp 15,s	;match desired exactly?;****    KLUDGE FOLLOWS:;	bne AroundDone****** 6 December 88	SMD* Fix bug where font got purged and was never reinstalled.  This happened* because the handle wasn't checked to see if it  was still valid (font not purged).*	ldy #8	lda [<IDPtr],y	;get info word to see if the font is on disk	and #NotDiskBit	;is font on disk?	beq SI0010	;yes;; If font is not on the disk, it was derived... lets check it out...	jsr CheckHandle	;do we have a handle to this font?	beq NextID	;no	jsr CheckNil	;yes - so check handle	beq NextID	;handle is nil - so	font was purged* end of bug fix******* Fixed bug 1/16/89	Mensch* Added label SI0010 and code above that branches to it so that installfont would* no longer ignore disk based fonts that were not loaded.*SI0010	lda <IDPtr	;save ptr to font	sta <BestPtr	lda <IDPtr+2	sta <BestPtr+2	lda <IDStyle	;save font's style	sta <BestStyle	lda <IDSize	;save font's size	sta <BestSize	bra DoneAroundDone		;;****    END OF THIS	KLUDGE - BHM  2/13/87	lda <IDPtr	;save ptr to font	sta <BestPtr	lda <IDPtr+2	sta <BestPtr+2	lda <IDStyle	;save font's style	sta <BestStyle	lda <IDSize	;save font's size	sta <BestSizeNextID	jsr IncIDPtr	;point to next ID entry	inc <Count	lda <Count	cmp <IDCount	;at end of list?	beq RetBest	;yes	brl IDLoopRetBest	lda <BestPtr	ora <BestPtr+2	;did we find a best	fit?	beq NoBestFound	;no	lda <BestPtr	;yes-set IDPtr to point to the best fit	sta <IDPtr	lda <BestPtr+2	sta <IDPtr+2Done	clc	;return with carry clear	rtsNoBestFound	sec	;return with carry set since	rts	;system font is best fit;------------------------------------------------------------------------------CountStyles	ldy #0	;count of # of styles set	ldx #8	;# bits left to checkLoop	lsr a	bcc NotSet	inyNotSet	dex	bne Loop	tya	;# of styles set	rts	ENDP****************************************************************** SetPurgeStat*****************************************************************	ENTRY SetPurgeStatSetPurgeStat	PROCPurgeState	equ Temp	phd	tcd	lda 11,s	;get fam #	tay	lda 13,s	;get style/size	jsr CheckFontID	bcc IDOK	brl StdErr6	;return errorIDOK	sta 13,s	;save converted style/size	tya	sta 11,s	;save converted fam	#	lda 9,s	;get purge setting	and #PurgeBit	;mask off other bits	sta <PurgeState	;and save	jsr LockIDList	ldx #0	;# of ID entries processed	ldy #2Loop	lda [<IDPtr]	;get fam #	cmp 11,s	;match?	bne NextID	;no	lda [<IDPtr],y	;get style/size	cmp 13,s	;match?	beq GotID	;yesNextID	jsr IncIDPtr	inx	cpx <IDCount	;at end of list?	bne Loop	;no	ldx #NoFontErr	;yes - so didn't find ID	bra RetErrGotID	lda <PurgeState	;check purge setting	beq Cont	;branch if setting is 'unpurgeable'	jsr CheckSysFont	;is this font the system font?	bne Cont	;no - so OK	ldx #PurgeErr	;yes - can't purge the system font	brl RetErrCont	jsr CheckHandle	;do we have a handle to this font?	beq NotInMem	;no - so error	jsr CheckNil	;is handle nil?	beq NotInMem	;yes - so error	ldy #8	lda [<IDPtr],y	;get font info	and #UnPurgeable	;clear PurgeBit	ora <PurgeState	;set correct purge state	sta [<IDPtr],y	;and save	lda <PurgeState	beq PushLevel	lda #2PushLevel	pha	;purge level	PushZLong <FontHandle	_SetPurge	;set purge level of	font	jsr UnLockIDList	brl StdEnd6NotInMem	ldx #MemErrRetErr	phx	;save error code	jsr UnLockIDList	;clean up	plx	;retrieve error code	brl StdErr6	;return the error	ENDP****************************************************************** CountFonts*****************************************************************	ENTRY CountFontsCountFonts	PROCDontUse	equ Temp	;these 2 bytes used	by FindFontStatsFindPos	equ DontUse+2Count	equ FindPos+2WantStyle	equ Count+2WantSize	equ WantStyle+2	phd	tcd	pha	;push 8 bytes of garbage on stack	pha	;so that params are	at same offsets	pha	;as params for FindFontStats and	pha	;LoadFont	jsr LockIDList	lda #$FFFF	;count all fonts	ENTRY CFCommonCFCommon	sta <FindPos	lda 19,s	;get fam #	bne NotZero	lda <SysFontID	;convert fam # of 0	to system fam #	sta 19,s	lda 21,s	;get style/size	bne NotZero	lda <SysFontID+2	sta 21,s	;convert to system font's style/sizeNotZero	lda 17,s	and #AnyFamBit	;is fam # important?	bne OK1	;no - so don't care if illegal #	lda 19,s	;get fam #	cmp #Illegal	;illegal #?	bne OK1	;no	ldx #FamNumErr	brl RetErr	;return errorOK1	lda 17,s	and #AnySizeBit	;is size important?	bne OK2	;no - so don't care if illegal value	lda 21,s	and #$FF00	;get size	bne OK2	;OK if not 0	ldx #SizeErr	brl RetErr	;return errorOK2	lda 21,s	and #$00FF	;get desired style	sta <WantStyle	;and save	lda 21,s	and #$FF00	;get desired size	sta <WantSize	;and save	stz <Count	ldx #0	;# of ID entries processedIDLoop	jsr CheckHandle	;do we have a handle to this font?	beq MemBitOK	;no - so font was never in mem	jsr CheckNil	;check for nil handle	bne MemBitOK	;not nil - so font is still in mem	ldy #8	;handle is nil - so	font was purged	lda [<IDPtr],y	;get info word	and #NotMemBit	;clear MemBit since	font not in mem	sta [<IDPtr],y	;and saveMemBitOK	ldy #8	lda [<IDPtr],y	;get info word	and #NotDiskBit	;is font on disk?	beq FontOK	;yes - so OK	lda [<IDPtr],y	;no - so font exists only in mem	and #MemBit	;is font still in mem?	beq NextID	;no - it's been purged so no goodFontOK	lda 17,s	and #MemOnlyBit	;count only fonts in mem?	beq MemOK	;no	ldy #8	lda [<IDPtr],y	;get info word	and #MemBit	;is font in mem?	beq NextID	;noMemOK	lda 17,s	and #RealOnlyBit	;count only real fonts?	beq RealOK	;no	ldy #8	lda [<IDPtr],y	;get info word	and #UnRealBit	;is font real?	bne NextID	;noRealOK	lda 17,s	and #AnyFamBit	;count any family?	bne FamOK	;yes	lda [<IDPtr]	;get fam #	cmp 19,s	;match?	bne NextID	;noFamOK	lda 17,s	and #AnySizeBit	;count any size?	bne SizeOK	;yes	ldy #2	lda [<IDPtr],y	and #$FF00	;get size	cmp <WantSize	;match?	bne NextID	;noSizeOK	ldy #2	lda [<IDPtr],y	and #$00FF	;get style	tay	;save temporarily	ora <WantStyle	cmp <WantStyle	;is it a subset of the desired style?	bne NextID	;no	lda 17,s	and #AnyStyleBit	;count any style?	bne StyleOK	;yes	cpy <WantStyle	;match?	bne NextID	;noStyleOK	inc <Count	;count this font	lda <Count	cmp <FindPos	;is this the font we are looking for?	bne NextID	;no	clc	;yes	rts	;return to FindFontStatsNextID	jsr IncIDPtr	inx	cpx <IDCount	;at end of list?	beq Done	;yes	brl IDLoopDone	lda <FindPos	cmp #$FFFF	;called by FindFontStats?	beq CountOK	;no	sec	;yes - so didn't find font	rts	;return to FindFontStats with errorCountOK	jsr UnLockIDList	pla	;clean garbage off stack	pla	pla	pla	lda <Count	sta 15,s	;return count	brl StdEnd6RetErr	phx	;save error code	jsr UnLockIDList	plx	;retrieve error code	pla	;pull return address off stack	lda <FindPos	cmp #$FFFF	;called by FindFontStats?	beq NotFFS	;no	ldy #12	;param size	jml errout	;return errorNotFFS	pla	;pull garbage off stack	pla	pla	brl StdErr6	;return error	ENDP****************************************************************** FindFontStats*** Change History** 15 Jul 88	Steven Glass** LoadTheFont trashes the d-page value TempPtr if the font is actually * loaded (not already in memory).  So we copy the pointer back off * the stack after calling LoadTheFont.*****************************************************************	ENTRY FindFontStatsFindFontStats	PROCLoadFlag	equ Temp	phd	tcd	lda #0	;don't load the font	ENTRY FFSCommonFFSCommon	sta <LoadFlag	lda 9,s	;get ptr to FontStatRec for output	sta <TempPtr	lda 11,s	sta <TempPtr+2	jsr LockIDList	lda 13,s	;position num to find	beq NoFont	;illegal position num	jsr CFCommon	bcc GotIt	;found the fontNoFont	lda #NotFoundBit	ldy #4	sta [<TempPtr],y	;signal font not found	bra DoneGotIt	lda <LoadFlag	;LoadFont call?	beq RetInfo	;no	lda #$FFFF	jsr LoadTheFont	;yes - so load the font into mem and	bcs RetErr	;make it the current fontRetInfo;; Copy the pointer to the fontstats record back onto d-page; (May have been trashed by LoadTheFont);	lda 9,s	;get ptr to FontStatRec for output	sta <TempPtr	lda 11,s	sta <TempPtr+2	lda [<IDPtr]	;return font ID	sta [<TempPtr]	ldy #2	lda [<IDPtr],y	sta [<TempPtr],y	ldy #8	lda [<IDPtr],y	;get font info word	ldy #4	sta [<TempPtr],y	;and returnDone	jsr UnLockIDList	ldy #12	;param size	jml endcallRetErr	phx	;save error code	jsr UnLockIDList	;clean up	plx	;retrieve error code	ldy #12	;param size	jml errout	;report the error	ENDP****************************************************************** LoadFont*****************************************************************	ENTRY LoadFontLoadFont	PROC	phd	tcd	lda #$FFFF	;load the font	brl FFSCommon	ENDP****************************************************************** LoadSysFont*****************************************************************	ENTRY LoadSysFontLoadSysFont	PROC	phd	tcd	jsr LockIDListLoop	jsr CheckSysFont	;is this font the system font?	beq FoundIt	;yes	jsr IncIDPtr	;no - so check next	ID entry	bra LoopFoundIt	lda #$FFFF	jsr LoadTheFont	;make system font the current font	jsr UnLockIDList	ldy #0	;param size	jml endcall	ENDP****************************************************************** AddFontVar*****************************************************************	ENTRY AddFontVarAddFontVar	PROCNewStats	equ TempNewIDSize	equ NewStats+2	phd	tcd	lda 9,s	;get new stats input for font	and #UnrealBit	;mask off all bits except UnrealBit	sta <NewStats	;and save for later	lda 11,s	;get handle to font	sta <FontHandle	lda 13,s	sta <FontHandle+2	jsr LockFont	jsr LockFamList	ldx #0	;# of fam entries checked	ldy #2FamLoop	lda [<FamPtr]	;get fam #	cmp [<FontPtr],y	;does it match font's fam #?	beq GotFam	;yes	jsr IncFamPtr	;no - so check next	fam entry	inx	cpx <FamCount	;at end of list?	bne FamLoop	;no	jsr UnLockFont	;yes	jsr UnLockFamList	ldx #NoFamErr	brl StdErr6	;return the errorGotFam	lda <IDListSize	;get current size of ID list	clc	adc #14	;add size of new entry	sta <NewIDSize	;and save	PushWord #0	;hi word of size	pha	;lo word of size	PushZLong <IDHandle	;handle to list	_SetHandleSize	;grow the list	bcc OK	pha	;save error code	jsr UnLockFont	;clean up	jsr UnLockFamList	plx	;retrieve error code	brl StdErr6	;report the errorOK	jsr LockIDList	clc	lda <IDPtr	;create ptr to new ID entry	adc <IDListSize	sta <IDPtr	lda <IDPtr+2	adc #0	sta <IDPtr+2	ldy #4	lda [<FontPtr],y	;get font's style word	and #$00FF	;mask off hi byte	pha	;save on stack	iny	iny	lda [<FontPtr],y	;get font's size word	and #$00FF	;mask off hi byte	xba	;swap bytes	ora 1,s	;OR with style word	ply	;clean up	ldy #2	sta [<IDPtr],y	;save style/size word in new ID entry	lda [<FamPtr]	;get fam #	sta [<IDPtr]	;and save in new ID	entry	lda [<FamPtr],y	;get offset to famname entry	iny	iny	sta [<IDPtr],y	;and save in new ID	entry	lda #0	iny	iny	sta [<IDPtr],y	;set filename offset to 0	ldy #4	lda [<FamPtr],y	;get fam info word	and #ApFamBit	;mask off all bits except ApFamBit	ora #ApVarBit	;set ApVarBit	ora #MemBit	;set MemBit	ora #NotDiskBit	;set NotDiskBit	ora <NewStats	;OR with NewStats	ldy #8	sta [<IDPtr],y	;and save in new ID	entry	iny	iny	lda 11,s	;get font handle	sta [<IDPtr],y	;and save in new ID	entry	iny	iny	lda 13,s	sta [<IDPtr],y	lda <NewIDSize	;get new size of ID	list	sta <IDListSize	;and save	inc <IDCount	;inc # of ID entries	Pushword #0	PushZLong <FontHandle	_SetPurge	;make font unpurgeable	jsr MakeCurrent	;make new font the current font	jsr UnLockFont	jsr UnLockIDList	jsr UnLockFamList	brl StdEnd6	ENDP****************************************************************** FMSetSysFont*****************************************************************	ENTRY FMSetSysFontFMSetSysFont	PROC	phd	tcd	lda 9,s	;get fam #	tay	lda 11,s	;get style/size	jsr CheckFontID	bcc IDOK	brl StdErr4	;return errorIDOK	sta 11,s	;save converted style/size	tya	sta 9,s	;save converted fam	#	jsr LockIDList	ldx #0	ldy #2Loop	lda [<IDPtr]	;get fam #	cmp 9,s	;match?	bne NextID	;no	lda [<IDPtr],y	;get style/size	cmp 11,s	;match?	beq FoundIt	;yesNextID	jsr IncIDPtr	;no - so check next	entry	inx	cpx <IDCount	;done with list?	bne Loop	;no	jsr UnLockIDList	;yes - so didn't find font	ldx #NoFontErr	brl StdErr4	;return the errorFoundIt	lda #notCurrFlag	jsr LoadTheFont	;load the font, don't make current	bcc OK	brl StdErr4	;return the errorOK	lda 9,s	;get fontID of new system font	sta <SysFontID	;and save	lda 11,s	sta <SysFontID+2	PushZLong <FontHandle	_SetSysFont	;tell QuickDraw about new sys font	jsr UnLockIDList	brl StdEnd4	ENDP****************************************************************** FMGetSysFID*****************************************************************	ENTRY FMGetSysFIDFMGetSysFID	PROC	phd	tcd	lda <SysFontID	;return font ID of system font	sta 9,s	lda <SysFontID+2	sta 11,s	ldy #0	;param size	jml endcall	ENDP****************************************************************** FMGetCurFID*****************************************************************	ENTRY FMGetCurFIDFMGetCurFID	PROCFontInfo	equ Temp	;the following items MUST appearFamNum	equ FontInfo	;in this orderStyle	equ FamNum+2Size	equ Style+2	phd	tcd	pha	;space for result	PushZPtr <FontInfo	;ptr to buffer for results	PushWord #6	;# bytes to return	_GetFontLore	;get info about current font	pla	;ignore result	lda <FamNum	;get font's fam #	sta 9,s	;and return	lda <Size	;get font's size	and #$00FF	;mask off hi byte	xba	;swap bytes	sta <Size	;and save	lda <Style	;get font's style	and #$00FF	;mask off hi byte	ora <Size	;OR with size	sta 11,s	;and return	ldy #0	;param size	jml endcall	ENDP****************************************************************** LoadTheFont*********************************************************************************************************	                  **  11/12/87  2:35 pm                  **	                  *********************************************************************************************************  MakeCurFlag renamed loadFlags, several control bits added*  for use with font scaling:**  bit 0:  currFlag*          0:  don't make font current*          1:  make	font current*  bit 1:  newMemFlag*          0:  make	newly-loaded-in font purgeable*          1:  make	it unpurgeable*  bit 2:  oldMemFlag*          0:  make	font found in memory purgeable*          1:  leave its purge status alone**    Bennet Marks  x6245  2/10/87**  NOTE/WARNING:  this routine leaves the loaded font unlocked.*  In the case of scaling, it may also leave it purgeable.	Any*  calling routine should be sure it doesn't let the font get*  purged accidentally before it uses it. - BHM  x6245  6/15/87**   Input: A*  Output: Carry flag****************************************************************	ENTRY LoadTheFontLoadTheFont	PROC	INCLUDE 'SomeFMEqus' ;added 2/12/87 - BHM*** added 2-Dec-91 DAL -- wrap SetSysPrefs around LoadTheFont	pha	jsr GetAndFixPrefs	pla	jsr RealLoadTheFont	php	_SetSysPrefsGS oldPrefs	plp	rtsGetAndFixPrefs	_GetSysPrefsGS oldPrefs	lda >oldPrefs+2	and #$dfff	;don't supress one-button dialogs	ora #$8000	;turn on prompt-for disk; keep Cancel state (7-Dec-91 DAL)	sta >myPrefs+2	_SetSysPrefsGS myPrefs	rtsoldPrefs	dc.w 1	;1 parameter	dc.w 0	;the old SysPrefsmyPrefs	dc.w 1	dc.w 0	;my modified preferencesRealLoadTheFont*** end 2-Dec-91 DAL	sta <loadFlags	jsr CheckHandle	;do we have a handle to this font?	beq NotInMem	;no - so load font in from disk	jsr CheckNil	;yes - so check if handle is nil	beq ItsPurged	;it's nil - so font was purged	jsr LockFont	;not nil - so font is in memory	bra InMem;font was in memory	but has been purgedItsPurged	jsr GetSizes	;open font file, get size info	bcc OK1	rts	;return error to calling routineOK1	PushZLong <FontHandle	_RestoreHandle	;restore the font handle	bcc LoadIt	;load the font into	mem	tax	;transfer error code to X	brl GotErr2;font was never in memoryNotInMem	jsr GetSizes	;open font file, get size info	bcc OK2	rts	;return error to calling routineOK2	lda <FontSize	;size of font in bytes	ldx <FontSize+2	;added 6-Jan-91 DAL	jsr GetHandleXA	;allocate space for	the font in mem	bcc GotHandle	brl GotErr2GotHandle	ldy #10	sta <FontHandle	sta [<IDPtr],y	;save handle to font in ID entry	iny	iny	txa	sta <FontHandle+2	sta [<IDPtr],y;load font into memory from diskLoadIt	jsr LockFont	;font file is open at this point	lda <FontPtr	sta <ReadPtr	;copy ptr to font area into READ params	lda <FontPtr+2	sta <ReadPtr+2	lda <FontSize	sta <ReadSize	;# of bytes to read***	stz <ReadSize+2	lda <FontSize+2	;6-Jan-91 DAL	sta <ReadSize+2	;6-Jan-91 DAL	jsr ReadFile	;load the font into	memory	stz <ReadSize+2	;6-Jan-91 DAL (just being paranoid, or maybe not)	bcs GotErr	jsr CloseFile	;close the font file	bcs GotErr;****  ALTERATIONS DONE TO HELP WITH FONT SCALING:;;font just brought into memory:	lda loadFlags	and #newMemFlag	bne MakeUnprgable;;make it purgeable:	ldy #8	lda [<IDPtr],y****  added for FontForADay - experimental - BHM  x6245  12/16/87	sta <oldStats	ora #(PurgeBit+MemBit) ;set purge and mem bits in list	sta [<IDPtr],y	PushWord #2	PushZLong <FontHandle	_SetPurge	;and make the font purgeable	bra PurgeStatDoneInMem;font was already in memory:	lda loadFlags	and #oldMemFlag	beq KeepPurgeStat	;leave purge status	alone;;otherwise, make it	unpurgeable:MakeUnprgable	ldy #8	lda [<IDPtr],y	;set mem bit, reset	purge bit****  added for FontForADay - experimental - BHM  x6245  12/16/87	sta <oldStats	and #Unpurgeable	ora #MemBit	sta [<IDPtr],y	PushWord #0	PushZLong <FontHandle	_SetPurge	;and make the font unpurgeable	bra PurgeStatDonePurgeStatDoneKeepPurgeStat	lda <loadFlags	and #currFlag	;make the font current?****  END OF ALTERATIONS - BHM  2/10/87	beq Done	;no	jsr MakeCurrent	;yesDone	jsr UnLockFont	clc	rtsGotErr	phx	;save error code	lxy <FontHandle	;8-Mar-93 SS	jsr DisposeTheHandle	;dispose of handle and font	plx	;retrieve error codeGotErr2	phx	;save error code	jsr CloseFile	;clean up	plx	;retrieve error code	sec	rts	;return to calling routine;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------GetSizes****changed to use FMParams block - BHM	 x6245  11/12/87	jsr LockFMParams	jsr LockFileList	ldy #6	clc	lda [<IDPtr],y	;get offset to filename entry	adc <FilePtr	;and create ptr to filename entry	sta <FilePtr	lda <FilePtr+2	adc #0	sta <FilePtr+2	jsr CopyFileName	;copy file name into pathname string	lda <FMParamPtr	clc	adc #(DirName-FMParams)	sta <OpenPtr	;store ptr to pathname of font file	lda <FMParamPtr+2	;in OPEN params	adc #0	sta <OpenPtr+2	jsr OpenFile	;open the font file	bcc OpenOK	phx	;save error code	jsr UnLockFileList	;clean up	jsr UnlockFMParams	plx	;retrieve error code	rts	;return the errorOpenOK	jsr UnLockFileList	jsr UnlockFMParams	jsr GetEOF	;get size of font file	lda <EOFSize	;might get trampled	by READ call	sta <currEOFSize	;but not here*** added 6-Jan-91 DAL	lda <EOFSize+2	sta <currEOFSize+2*** end of 6-Jan-91 DAL addition	bcs RetErr	jsr LockNameList	ldy #4	lda [<IDPtr],y	;get offset to famname	tay	lda [<NamePtr],y	;get length of famname	and #$00FF	;mask off hi byte	inc a	;add 1 for the length byte itself	sta <NameSize	;save for later	jsr UnLockNameList	lda <NameSize	cmp #MaxNameLen+1	;is name length = max name length?	bne GotNameLen	;no - so we have the correct length;;we are about to read the font file's first 2 bytes into the;0-page location NameSize  (it's weird, but what the hey?);(changed from an even weirder form 11/12/87 - BHM  x6245)	tdc	clc	adc #NameSize	sta <ReadPtr	;point to that 0-page location	stz <ReadPtr+2	;high word 0, of course	lda #2	;# bytes to read	sta <ReadSize	stz <ReadSize+2	jsr ReadFile	;read first word of	font file	bcs RetErr	lda <NameSize	;get name length	and #$00FF	;mask off hi byte	inc a	;add 1 for length byte itself	sta <NameSize	;and saveGotNameLen	sec	lda <currEofSize	sbc <NameSize	;calculate size of the font file not	sta <FontSize	;including the famname*** added 6-Jan-91 DAL	lda <currEofSize+2	sbc #0	sta <FontSize+2*** end of 6-Jan-91 DAL addition	lda <NameSize	sta <MarkLoc	stz <MarkLoc+2	jsr SetMark	;set current position of file to start	bcs RetErr	;of font	clc	rtsRetErr	phx	;save error code	jsr CloseFile	;clean up	plx	;retrieve error code	sec	rts	ENDP****************************************************************** InstallWithStats**    (name changed from FontForADay 1/4/88 - BHM  x6245*****************************************************************;****************************************	                  **  1/4/88 3:45 pm	                  **	                  ****************************************;*****************************************************************  This call combines features of InstallFont and FindFontStats.*  It does a normal	InstallFont, but it	also returns a FontStatRec*  reflecting the status that the font that is installed (the font*  ACTUALLY installed - not necessarily	the font asked for)	had*  BEFORE this call	was made.  It is intended to be used for saving*  and restoring the status of a font (particularly its purge status)**  Bennet Marks  x6245****************************************************************;	ENTRY InstallWithStatsInstallWithStats	PROC	;my longest label!;FontInfo	equ TempFamNum	equ FontInfoStyle	equ FamNum+2Size	equ Style+2ErrCode1	equ Size+2;	phd	tcd;	lda 13,s	;scaleWord	tax	lda 15,s	;famNum	tay	lda 17,s	;style/size	pha	phy	phx;	jsl xInstallFont;	sta <ErrCode1	;error code, if any;	pha	;space for result	PushZPtr <FontInfo	PushWord #6	;number of bytes to	get	_GetFontLore	pla	;result - we don't use it;	lda 9,s	sta <tempPtr	lda 11,s	sta <tempPtr+2;	lda <FamNum	sta [<tempPtr]	lda <Size	and #$00FF	xba	sta <Size	lda <Style	and #$00FF	ora <Size	ldy #2	sta [<tempPtr],y;	lda <oldStats	ldy #4	sta [<tempPtr],y;	ldx <ErrCode1	bne Err1;no error:	ldy #10	clc	ldy #10	jml endcall;Err1	ldy #10	sec	jml errout;xInstallFont	tdc	jsl InstallFont	rtl	ENDP;                COPY mdstuff**************************************************************** FixFontMenu*****************************************************************	ENTRY FixFontMenuFixFontMenu	PROC;****  Changed for purposes of ROMmability - BHM  x6245  12/10/87**** many changes noted by a "*" for ease of debugging;MenuID	equ TempNumNames	equ MenuID+2	phd	tcd	jsr LockFMParams	;must be called before BuildMDList, because BuildMDList 		;was using the FMParamPtr stored in zero page, after 		;the handle was unlocked, yet it is possible that 		;this pointer might have been moved because of compaction		;or something(4/28/88, HY)	jsr BuildMDList	;build list of ptrs	to famnames	bcc OK	jsr unLockFMParams	brl StdErr6	;return the errorOK	jsr LockMDList	lda 13,s	;get menu ID	sta <MenuID	lda 11,s	;get starting item ID	sta <StartingID	ldy #(DummyItemID-FMParams)	sta [<FMParamPtr],y	;*store starting item ID in dummy item	ldy #(MDListSize-FMParams)	lda [<FMParamPtr],y	;*get # of entries in MD list	sta <NumNames	;and saveLoop;push pointer to dummy menu item:	ldx <FMParamPtr+2	;*high word	lda <FMParamPtr	clc	adc #(DummyItem-FMParams)	bcc NoCarry1	inxNoCarry1	phx	pha	PushWord #$FFFF	;append to end of menu	PushZWord <MenuID	;push menu ID	_InsertMItem	;append dummy menu item to end of menu	ldy #2	lda [<MDPtr],y	;push ptr to famname	pha	lda [<MDPtr]	pha	ldy #(DummyItemID-FMParams)	lda [<FMParamPtr],y	pha	;*push item ID of dummy item just added	_SetMItemName	;replace 'Dummy' with famname	jsr IncMDPtr	;point to next MD list entry*increment item ID for next famname	ldy #(DummyItemID-FMParams)	lda [<FMParamPtr],y	inc a	sta [<FMParamPtr],y	dec <NumNames	;done with all famnames?	bne Loop	;no;Convert the list of ptrs to famnames (MDList) into a list of family;numbers (ItemList)	which are in the same order as the font	famnames;in the menu.  ItemList is used by the ItemID2FamNum routine.	lda <MenuMade	;was an ItemList created previously?	beq Cont	;no	lxy <ItemHandle ;yes - so release	the space	jsr DisposeTheHandle	;8-Mar-93 SSCont	lda <MDHandle	;copy handle to MD list	sta <ItemHandle	lda <MDHandle+2	sta <ItemHandle+2	jsr LockMDList	;reset MDPtr back to start of list	jsr LockItemList	;set up ItemPtr to also point to list	ldy #(MDListSize-FMParams)	lda [<FMParamPtr],y	;*get # of entries in MD list	sta <NumNames	;and saveItemLoop	ldy #6	lda [<MDPtr],y	;get fam # corresponding to famname ptr	sta [<ItemPtr]	;and move up	jsr IncMDPtr	;point to next MD list entry	jsr IncItemPtr	;point to next Item	list entry	dec <NumNames	;done?	bne ItemLoop	;no	jsr UnLockMDList	PushWord #0	;hi word of new size	ldy #(MDListSize-FMParams)	lda [<FMParamPtr],y	;*get # of items in	MD list	asl a	;multiply by 2 to get size of Item list	pha	;lo word of size		;** code added 2-25-87 CAE **	sta <ItemListSize	;save size of Item list		;** end addition **	PushZLong <MDHandle	;handle to list	_SetHandleSize	;shrink MD list to use as Item list	inc <MenuMade	;set flag so Names list will stay locked		;since menu contains ptrs to famnames	jsr UnlockFMParams	brl StdEnd6	ENDP****************************************************************** ItemID2FamNum*****************************************************************	ENTRY ItemID2FamNumItemID2FamNum	PROC	phd	tcd	lda <MenuMade	bne OK	ldx #MenuErr	;FixFontMenu never calledErrRet	ldy #2	;param size	jml errout	;return the errorOK	jsr LockItemList	sec	lda 9,s	;get item ID	sbc <StartingID	;create offset into	Item list	asl a	tay;		;** code added 2-25-87 CAE **	cpy <ItemListSize	;past end of list?	bcc OK2	;no - so OK	jsr UnLockItemList	;yes - so unlock list	ldx #NoFamErr	;and return error	bra ErrRet;		;** end addition **OK2	lda [<ItemPtr],y	;get fam # corresponding to item ID	sta 11,s	;and return	jsr UnLockItemList	ldy #2	;param #	jml endcall	ENDP****************************************************************** FamNum2ItemID*****************************************************************	ENTRY FamNum2ItemIDFamNum2ItemID	PROC	phd	tcd	lda <MenuMade	bne OK	ldx #MenuErr	;FixFontMenu never calledErrRet	ldy #2	;param size	jml errout	;return the errorOK	jsr LockItemList	ldy #0Loop	lda [<ItemPtr],y	;get fam #	cmp 9,s	;is it the one we're looking for?	beq GotIt	;yes	iny	;no - so check next	entry	iny	cpy <ItemListSize	;at end of list?	bcc Loop	;no	jsr UnLockItemList	;yes - so unlock list	ldx #NoFamErr	;and return error	bra ErrRetGotIt	tya	;get offset into list	lsr a	;and divide by 2	clc	adc <StartingID	;and add to starting item ID	sta 11,s	;to create item ID for this fam #	jsr UnLockItemList	ldy #2	;param size	jml endcall	ENDP**********************************************************************************	    * ChooseFont * Version 2.5	        *	    * Copyright Apple Computer, Inc. 1986-1988              * All Rights Reserved                   *	    * V2.5  1/4/89	Mensch** **************************************************************************************************************************************************** ChooseFont*****************************************************************	ENTRY ChooseFontChooseFont	PROC;****  EXPERIMENTAL CHANGE:;only CurNum, CurStyle, and CurSize need to survive the call to InstallFont.;By moving them to the end, and letting	other ChooseFont temporary 0-page;locations overlap with InstallFont's, we can reclaim some 0-page, which;will be put to good use.  Trust me.  BHM  x6245  11/3/87;****  Changed to accomodate ROMming - BHM  x6245  12/10/87****  many changes marked with a "*" for ease of debugging;;; Changed to handle	updating manually 1/3/89 Mensch;; Changed to use NewWindow2 templates 1/5/89 Mensch; This change will allow personalization/internationalization of this dialog box; and its asociated alert.*** TaskRec	equ Temp	;must be first!*** TempStyle	equ TaskRec+24*** TempStyle	equ TempTempStyle	equ Temp+24	;24-Feb-91 DAL (I can't use less direct-page space than before!!)CntlHndl	equ TempStyle+2CntlHndls	equ CntlHndl+4	;these 3 items must	be in this orderPlainHndl	equ CntlHndlsStyleHndls	equ PlainHndl+4LinePtr	equ StyleHndls+20Count	equ LinePtr+4Index	equ Count+2CancelFlag	equ Index+2;; It is vital that, at this point, we're beyond the end of; IntallFont's temporary 0-page  (which we are) - BHM  11/3/87;CurNum	equ CancelFlag+2CurStyle	equ CurNum+2CurSize	equ CurStyle+2;; Storage for the handles of our listMDCtlHandle	equ CurSize+2SizeCtlHandle	equ MDCtlHandle+4	phd	tcd	jsr LockFMParams	stz <CancelFlag	jsr BuildMDList	;build list of ptrs	to famnames	bcc OK	brl StdErr6	;return the errorOK	lda 11,s	;get fam #	tay	lda 13,s	;get style/size	jsr CheckFontID	bcc IDOK	brl StdErr6	;return errorIDOK	sta 13,s	;save converted style/size	tya	sta 11,s	;save converted fam	#	sta <CurNum	;save current fam #	lda 13,s	and #$00FF	;get current style	sta <CurStyle	;and save	lda 13,s	and #$FF00	;get current size	xba	sta <CurSize	;and save*	phb	;save data bank register	phk	plb	;set data bank to program bank	pha	;space for result	pha	_GetPort	;save current port on stack	stz <ScreenMode	;init to 320 mode	pha	;space for result	_GetMasterSCB	pla	and #$0080	;is bit 7 set?	beq Its320	;no - so in 320 mode	lda #8	;yes - so in 640 mode	sta <ScreenMode	;set to 8 to index rects correctlyIts320		;*	jsr LockMDList*copy the pointer to MD list into the list record for MD list	lda <MDPtr	ldy #(MDListPtr-FMParams)	sta [<FMParamPtr],y	lda <MDPtr+2	iny	iny	sta [<FMParamPtr],y	jsr DrawDialog	;draw the dialog boxLoopTask	pha	pha	;space for DoModalWindow result	pushlong #TaskRec	ldx #0	phx	phx	;custom update	lda #^(cfEventHook+$80000000) ;EventHook: bit 31 = Apple-period --> ESC	pha	pea cfEventHook	phx	phx	;Beep proc	pea $9	;flags (xxx+noScrapForLE)	_DoModalWindow	pla	plx	tay	beq LoopTask	;nothing hit*** (A = control ID low word; this is important)*** added 4-Oct-91 DAL -- if they just hit a Tab, don't rebuild the size list	tax	lda TaskRec	cmp #keyDownEvt	beq @isKey	cmp #autoKeyEvt	bne @notKey@isKey	lda TaskRec+2	;message field	and #$00ff	cmp #$0009	;Tab?	beq LoopTask@notKey	txa*** end 4-Oct-91	pha	pha	;space for GetCtlHandleFromID result	pha	pha	;space for FrontWindow result	_FrontWindow	lda 5,s	;retrieve copy of control ID (low word)	pea 0	pha	_GetCtlHandleFromID	pla	sta <cntlHndl	pla	sta <cntlHndl+2	pha	_MWGetCtlPart	pla	cmp #ListPartCode	;was the hit on a list control?	beq OKControl	;yes  - so OK	cmp #5	;was the hit on a standard control?	bcc OKControl	;yes - so OKInCont10	brl LoopTask	;no - so get next eventOKControl	pha	;space for result	pha	PushZLong <CntlHndl	;control handle	_GetCtlRefCon	;get address of routine to handle hit	pla	; low word...	plx	; high word	bne OKCByPtr	; passed refcon is a routine pointer	cmp #10	; test to see if the passed routine is standard	bge OKCByPtr	; if not, the assume by pointer	asl a	; multiply the refcon by 2	tax	; use it as an index	lda >handlerTbl,x	; get the address from handler table 	OKCByPtr; this routine JSRs to the routine pointer to by the refcon. 	dec a	pha	;push address on stack	rts	;return into routineOKC_Dummy			brl LoopTaskhandlerTbl; table of routines that handle various controls in our dialog. This table MUST have ; 16 entries in it!	dc.W OKC_Dummy	; 0 - Do nothing	dc.W FontHit	; 1 - Handle a hit in the font list	dc.W SizeHit	; 2 - Handle hit in size list	dc.w OKC_Dummy	; 3 - hit the other-size box (DAL)	dc.W OKHit	; 4 - hit in OK button	dc.W CancelHit	; 5 - hit in cancel button	dc.W PlainHit	; 6 - hit in plain style item	dc.W StyleHit	; 7 - hit in other style item	dc.W OKC_Dummy	; 8 - nothing	dc.W OKC_Dummy	; 9 - nothing	dc.W OKC_Dummy	; 10 - nothing	dc.W OKC_Dummy	; 11 - nothing	dc.W OKC_Dummy	; 12 - nothing	dc.W OKC_Dummy	; 13 - nothing	dc.W OKC_Dummy	; 14 - nothing	dc.W OKC_Dummy	; 15 - nothing	;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------;; The hit was in the OK button;	Entry OKHitOKHit	jsr GetNewSize	;get new font size	lda <CurSize	bne SizeNotZero	;size of zero not allowedBadSize	jsr DoAlert	;put up alert box	brl LoopTaskSizeNotZero	cmp #256	bcs BadSize	;size > 255 not allowed; get selected font style	stz <CurStyle	ldx #(5*4)-4	;index to last style controlStyleLoop	asl <CurStyle	phx	;save X	pha	;space for result	lda <StyleHndls+2,x	;handle to control	pha	lda <StyleHndls,x	pha	_GetCtlValue	;get current value of control	pla	beq DoNext	;branch if not set	inc <CurStyle	;set bit corresponding to the styleDoNext	plx	;retrieve X	dex	dex	dex	dex	;set index to next style control	bpl StyleLoop; finish upFinishUp	PushZLong <WindPtr	_CloseWindow	;close window	_InitCursor	;added 5-Feb-92 DAL	lxy <MDHandle	;8-Mar-93 SS	jsr DisposeTheHandle	;dispose of MD list	jsr UnLockNameList	jsr UnlockFMParams	_SetPort	;restore port	plb	;restore data bank register	lda <CancelFlag	;was Cancel hit?	bne Done	;yes; compare selected fontID against original fontID	lda <CurSize	;create style/size word	xba	ora <CurStyle	tay	;and save	cmp 13,s	;compare with original style/size	bne InstallNew	;different so install new font	lda <CurNum	cmp 11,s	;compare fam #	bne InstallNew	;different so install new font	bra Done	;new font = old font, so no change; new font is different from old font so install itInstallNew	phy	;style/size	PushZWord <CurNum	;fam #	PushWord #0	;enable scaling;; 1/5/90 Mensch;; Added code here that idle's the cursor for the instal font call.; this puts up the watch cursor when needed.;	pha	pha	_GetCursorAdr	pla	sta <WindPtr	; use wind pointer to store temp value	pla	sta <WindPtr+2		_WaitCursor	; put up the watch cursor...		_InstallFont	;install font	PushzLong <WindPtr	; put the cursor back...	_SetCursor	; return selected fontIDDone	lda <CurNum	sta 15,s	lda <CurSize	xba	ora <CurStyle	sta 17,s	brl StdEnd6;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------;; The hit was in the Cancel button;	Entry CancelHitCancelHit	stz <CurNum	;return 0 as selected font ID	stz <CurSize	stz <CurStyle	inc <CancelFlag	brl FinishUp;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------;; The hit was in the 'Plain' check box;	Entry PlainHitPlainHit	PushWord #1	;control value	PushZLong <PlainHndl ;control handle	_SetCtlValue	;set the control	ldx #(5*4)-4	;index to last Style controlClearLoop	phx	PushWord #0	;new control value	lda <StyleHndls+2,x	pha	;control handle	lda <StyleHndls,x	pha	_SetCtlValue	;clear out all Style check boxes	plx	dex	dex	dex	dex	;set index to next Style control	bpl ClearLoop	brl LoopTask;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------;; The hit was in one of the Style check boxes (other than the 'Plain' check box);	Entry StyleHitStyleHit	PushWord #0	PushZLong <PlainHndl	_SetCtlValue	;clear out 'Plain' check box*** added 4-Oct-91 DAL** Are there any style boxes checked?  If not, re-check the plain box.*	ldx #4*4	;5 control handles to check@checkThemBoxes	phx	pha	;space for GetCtlValue	lda <StyleHndls+2,x	pha	lda <StyleHndls,x	pha	_GetCtlValue	pla	;get check-box state	plx	;restore ctl id counter	tay	bne @oneIsChecked	dex	dex	dex	dex	bpl @checkThemBoxes; nothing checked --> check the Plain box	pea 1	;new ctl value	pei <PlainHndl+2	pei <PlainHndl	_SetCtlValue	;check the Plain box@oneIsChecked*** end 4-Oct-91	brl LoopTask;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------;; The hit was in the list of font family names;	ENTRY FontHitFontHit	jsr GetNewSize	;get latest font size setting	pha	;space for result	Pushword #0	;start at member 0	pushZLong <MDCtlHandle	_NextMember2	pla	; member number to select	beq FontHitDone	;no member was selected;; Now that we have the item number, we must turn it into an address;	dec a	; subtract 1 (we base list off zero)	ldy #2	; init our index...		asl a	; multiply the member by 8	asl a	asl a	clc	; and prepare to create a member pointer	adc [<MDHandle]	sta <MDPtr	; and save it as our pointer	lda [<MDHandle],y	adc #0	sta <MDPtr+2		ldy #6	lda [<MDPtr],y	;get fam # of selected member	sta <CurNum	;and save	jsr BuildSizeList	;update the list of	font sizes toFontHitDone	brl LoopTask	;correspond to this	fam #;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------;; The hit was in the list of font sizes;	ENTRY SizeHitSizeHit	pha	;space for result	Pushword #0	;start at member 0	pushZLong <SizeCtlHandle	_NextMember2	pla	; member number to select	beq SizeHitDone	;no member was selected; Now multiply the item number by 5	dec A	; subtract 1 to offset for 0 starting list	sta <temp1Ptr	; save the item number for a sec...	asl a	; multiply it by 4	asl a	clc	adc <temp1Ptr	; we now have (ItemNo-1)*5 in <A>	clc	adc #(SizeList-FMParams) ; offset into our data area	clc	; now create the actual pointer	adc <FMParamPtr	sta <temp1Ptr	; after all that, this is a pointer to our item	lda <FMParamPtr+2	adc #0	sta <temp1Ptr+2	lda [<temp1Ptr]	;get size from selected member	sta <CurSize	;and save	jsr MakeString	;convert size into a string	jsr SetSizeText	;set the 'Other Size' text to the string	jsr SelectSizeText	;select the 'Other Size' text	pha	pha	PushZLong <LineHndl	;handle to LineEdit	record	_GetCtlTitle	_LEUpdate	;redraw the textSizeHitDone	brl LoopTask** cfEventHook** Input: event record pointer on stack*cfEventHook	phd	tsc	tcd; event pointer is at 6	lda [6]	cmp #3	beq @key	cmp #5	bne @notKey@key	ldy #2	lda [6],y	and #$00ff	cmp #9	;Tab is always OK	beq @noProblem	cmp #$0d	;Return is okay	beq @noProblem	cmp #$1b	;Escape is okay	beq @noProblem	pha	pha	;space for GetCtlID	pha	pha	;space for FindTargetCtl	_FindTargetCtl	_GetCtlID	pla	plx	cmp #MDListID	beq @noProblem	cmp #SizeListID	bne @notSzList	jsr AllowArrowsOnly	bra @notKey; they must be at the Edit line control@notSzList	ldy #2	lda [6],y	and #$00ff	cmp #$08	;left arrow	beq @OKChar	cmp #$15	;right arrow	beq @OKChar	cmp #$7F	;delete	beq @OKChar	cmp #$18	;control-X	beq @OKChar	cmp #$06	;control-F	beq @OKChar	cmp #$19	;control-Y	beq @OKChar	cmp #'0'	bcc @BadChar	cmp #'9'+1	bcc @OKChar@badChar	jsr SelectFamilyList@noProblem@okChar@notKey	pld	lda 2,s	sta 2+4,s	lda 1,s	sta 1+4,s	pla	pla	rtlAllowArrowsOnly	ldy #2	lda [6],y	and #$00ff	cmp #$000a	beq @ok	cmp #$000b	bne SelectFamilyList@ok	rtsSelectFamilyList	pha	pha	pea 0	pea 0	pushlong #MDListID	_GetCtlHandleFromID	_MakeThisCtlTarget	rts;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------;; Create the dialog window and then draw it;DrawDialog	pha	pha	; room for result	PushWord #$800E	; resource type to load	ldx <ScreenMode	; get the current screen mode	lda WindTemplates+2,x ; and pass the pointer to the template 	pha	lda WindTemplates,x ; and pass the pointer to the template 	pha	_GetRomResource	PullLong <WindPtr; lock the handle we got back...	ldy #4	lda [<WindPtr],y	; get the flags byte	ora #$8000	; lock it	sta [<WindPtr],y	; and put it back...		ldy #2	; now dereference the handle	lda [<WindPtr],y	tax	lda [<WindPtr]	sta <WindPtr	stx <WindPtr+2	ldx #0	phx	phx	; room for result	phx	phx	; no title	phx	phx	; no refcon	PushLong #DrawGuts	; address of draw routine	phx	phx	; DefProcPtr	phx	; Reference descriptor	pushzLong <WindPtr	pea $800E	; use an rWindparam1 window	_NewWindow2	; create the window and controls	pla	;get ptr to window and save	sta <WindPtr	;in zero page	pla	sta <WindPtr+2	PushWord #$800E	; resource type to load	ldx <ScreenMode	; get the current screen mode	lda WindTemplates+2,x ; and pass the pointer to the template 	pha	lda WindTemplates,x ; and pass the pointer to the template 	pha	_ReleaseRomResource	PushZLong <WindPtr	_SetPort;; Now, update the contents of the lists for later use;; Get the MD list's ctrl handle so we can update it	pha	; room for result	pha	pei <WindPtr+2	pei <WindPtr	PushLong #MDListID	_GetCtlHandleFromID	pla	sta <MDCtlHandle	pla	sta <MDCtlHandle+2	; get the control handle		ldx #0	; now set MD list to use the already created data	phx	; negative 1...	phx	; Pointer to draw routine	pea 1	; leave same thing selected	pei <MDHandle+2	pei <MDHandle	pea 1	; ref verb zero means pass by ptr, 1 means by handle	ldy #(MDListSize-FMParams)	lda [<FMParamPtr],y	; get number of list members	pha	pei <MDCtlHandle+2	pei <MDCtlHandle	_NewList2	; create the MD list;make the correct font family name selected		ldy #(MDListSize-FMParams)	lda [<FMParamPtr],y	;*  # of list members	sta <CountSelLoop	ldy #6	lda [<MDPtr],y	;get fam #	cmp <CurNum	;current family?	beq SelMember	;yes	jsr IncMDPtr	;no - so check next	member	dec <Count	;done with list?	bne SelLoop	;no	bra NoSelSelMember	ldy #(MDListSize-FMParams)	lda [<FMParamPtr],y	;# of list members	sec	sbc <Count	; now select the proper member	inc a	pha	pei <MDCtlHandle+2	pei <MDCtlHandle	_SelectMember2	; and select the current fontNoSel; create the list of font sizes and select the current size	pha	; room for result	pha	pei <WindPtr+2	pei <WindPtr	PushLong #SizeListID	_GetCtlHandleFromID	pla	sta <SizeCtlHandle	; get the control handle	pla	sta <SizeCtlHandle+2		lda #1	ldy #(SizeListSize-FMParams)	sta [<FMParamPtr],y	;init to 1 member	jsr BuildSizeList	;create Size list, select current size	pha	; room for result	pha	pei <WindPtr+2	pei <WindPtr	PushLong #SizeEditID	_GetCtlHandleFromID	pla	sta <LineHndl	;save the handle on	zero page	pla	sta <LineHndl+2	ldx #PlainSID	stz <Index; get all the style checkbox control handlesGetStylehndl	phx		pha	; room for result	pha	pei <WindPtr+2	pei <WindPtr	pea 0	phx	_GetCtlHandleFromID	ldx <Index	; load the index offset...	pla	sta <CntlHndls,x	;save the handle on	zero page	pla	sta <CntlHndls+2,x	lda <Index	clc	adc #4	sta <Index	plx	inx	cpx #LastSID	; is it the last ID?	blt GetStyleHndl; convert the current font's size to a string	lda <CurSize	;get current font size	jsr MakeString	;convert into a string	jsr SetSizeText	;set the 'Other Size' text to the string	jsr SelectSizeText	;select the 'Other Size' text; get the style of the current font and set the Style check boxes accordingly	lda <CurStyle	;get current style	beq SetPlain	;branch if 'Plain'	sta <TempStyle	;save current style	lda #5	sta <Count	;# of 'Style' check	boxes	ldx #0	;start at first 'Style' check boxSetStyles	phx	lsr <TempStyle	;check style bit	bcc NotSet	;branch if not set	PushWord #1	;new control value	lda <StyleHndls+2,x	;handle to correct check box	pha	lda <StyleHndls,x	pha	_SetCtlValue	;set the check boxNotSet	plx	inx	inx	inx	inx	;index next check box	dec <Count	bne SetStyles	brl ShowItSetPlain	PushWord #1	PushZLong <PlainHndl	_SetCtlValue	;set the 'Plain' check boxShowIt	PushZLong <WindPtr	;ptr to window	_ShowWindow	;draw the window	rts;------------------------------------------------------------------------------;; Create list of sizes available for the currently selected font family.; Sort the list in numerical order.; Select the current size if available and then draw the new list.;BuildSizeList; create the list of font sizes	jsr LockIDList;	lda #0	ldy #(SizeListSize-FMParams)	sta [<FMParamPtr],y	sta <Count;	lda <FMParamPtr	clc	adc #(SizeList-FMParams)	sta <temp1Ptr;*  added 1/14/88 - let's get the size list structure right - BHM  x6245;	lda <FMParamPtr+2	adc #0	sta <temp1Ptr+2;; in this ROMmable version, we'll use y for actual indexing, but x; for index calculations;	ldx #0BuildLoop	lda [<IDPtr]	;get fam #	cmp <CurNum	;match?	bne NextID	;no;       ;** code added 2-25-87 CAE **	ldy #8	lda [<IDPtr],y	;get info word	and #UnRealBit	;was this font scaled from another font?	bne NextID	;yes - so don't list it	ldy #2;       ;** end addition **	lda [<IDPtr],y	and #$FF00	;get size	xba	txy	sta [<temp1Ptr],y	;and store in list member	inx	inx	inx	inx	inx	;set index to next Size list member	ldy #(SizeListSize-FMParams)	lda [<FMParamPtr],y	inc a	;increment number of members in list	sta [<FMParamPtr],y	cmp #MaxSListCount	;is Size list full?	beq BuildDone	;yesNextID	jsr IncIDPtr	;point to next ID entry	inc <Count	lda <Count	cmp <IDCount	;done with ID list?	bne BuildLoop	;noBuildDone	jsr UnLockIDList; setup the record with the current info	jsr doNewList; sort the list	PushPtr SortSizes	;address of routine	to sort members	pei <SizeCtlHandle+2	pei <SizeCtlHandle	_SortList2*** added 9-Mar-93 SS **** Now, the list was built without checking for duplicate sizes, which it can have if* there are multiple styles in the same size.  So, shrink out the duplicates...		pei <temp1Ptr+2		pei <temp1Ptr	ldy #(SizeListSize-FMParams)	lda [<FMParamPtr],y	;# of items in list	pha	lda #0	;init the indexes and counters to zero	pha	pha	pha	pha	phd	tsc	tcddSrc	equ 3	;src indexdDest	equ 5	;dest indexdNewCount	equ 7	;new shrunk countdCount	equ 9	;old unshrunk countdTotal	equ 11	;gross total in unshrunk listd